{"parentUuid":"efa77e89-e428-4ff6-9b0f-348ef3180b3b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5115a40f-3bbe-4e18-b349-376c9f5882f9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AXmqv29ZANJ7hU3o14EkEz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: prompt\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** drafting\n4\t**Authors:** claude-code, codex\n5\t**Created:** 2026-05-08\n6\t\n7\t## TLDR\n8\t\n9\tShip `entire investigate` as a hidden top-level command surfaced through\n10\t`entire labs`. It runs a non-TUI marvin-style round-robin loop across\n11\tlaunchable, hook-enabled agents (claude-code, codex, gemini-cli), bootstraps\n12\ta findings doc + timeline (including prior Entire context when there is no\n13\tseed doc), and tags each spawned session with a new `agent_investigate` Kind\n14\tso the next commit condenses the investigation into `entire/checkpoints/v1`\n15\talongside `entire review` runs. GitHub issue/PR URLs seed the loop through\n16\t`gh`; a local manifest plus an `entire investigate fix` helper lets users feed\n17\taccepted findings into a follow-up coding session. Biggest tradeoff:\n18\tinvestigate gets its own `HasInvestigation` umbrella flag and\n19\t`Kind.IsInvestigate()` predicate rather than reusing review's umbrella, so the\n20\tfeature stays semantically honest at the cost of updating every local reader\n21\tthat currently only knows about review.\n22\t\n23\t## Problem / Motivation\n24\t\n25\t`marvin investigate` (POC at `/Users/alisha/Projects/marvin`) runs a\n26\tmulti-agent investigation against a seeded question or doc and produces a\n27\tfindings + timeline artifact. We want to graduate that workflow into the\n28\tEntire CLI as a real, supported command — `entire investigate` — that reuses\n29\tthe `entire review` scaffolding so investigations are saved, linked to\n30\tcheckpoints, and condensed onto `entire/checkpoints/v1` the same way reviews\n31\tare. Today nothing in `entire` captures pre-implementation investigation\n32\twork; ad-hoc agent runs lose their context on the next commit, and there is\n33\tno provenance trail tying \"we investigated X\" to the commit it informed.\n34\t\n35\tInvestigations also need to be triggerable from external work tracking. The\n36\tuser should be able to point the command at a GitHub issue or PR (or any\n37\tcode-issue link) and have it pull the linked content as the seed, without\n38\thand-copying the issue body into a doc.\n39\t\n40\t## Goals\n41\t\n42\t- Add a new `entire investigate` command that mirrors `entire review`'s\n43\t  placement: top-level command, listed under `entire labs` as experimental,\n44\t  invoked directly (no `entire labs investigate` namespace).\n45\t- Reuse `entire review` scaffolding for persistence and provenance: an\n46\t  `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` env-var handshake parallel to `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*`,\n47\t  lifecycle adoption to tag the session, an `attach` subcommand,\n48\t  condensation onto `entire/checkpoints/v1` via the existing multi-session\n49\t  checkpoint format, and a new `HasInvestigation` umbrella flag on\n50\t  `CheckpointSummary`.\n51\t- Match the `marvin investigate` UX where it makes sense: accept either a\n52\t  `--topic` (matching marvin's `--question`) or a `[seed-doc]` positional\n53\t  path, port marvin's investigate prompt body verbatim, drive a round-robin\n54\t  loop with stances and quorum, and persist a findings doc + timeline.\n55\t- Add a `--issue-link <url>` flag that accepts GitHub issue and PR URLs\n56\t  (resolved via `gh issue|pr view --json`), turns the issue body into a\n57\t  seed findings doc, and falls back with a clear \"save to a file and pass\n58\t  as a positional `[seed-doc]`\" error for unsupported hosts.\n59\t- Provide a way to feed a saved investigation back into a follow-up agent\n60\t  run: `entire investigate fix [<run-id>]` mirrors `entire review --fix` —\n61\t  resolves the manifest, composes a prompt that says \"use these findings\n62\t  as context, do not re-investigate\", and launches a regular coding agent\n63\t  session.\n64\t- Persist the findings as part of checkpoint metadata and local manifests so\n65\t  `entire status`, `entire checkpoint explain --json`, and\n66\t  `entire investigate --findings` / `fix` can surface them. Dedicated\n67\t  `entire search` investigation UX is out of scope for this PR because it\n68\t  depends on the cloud search service, not only this CLI repo.\n69\t\n70\t## Non-Goals\n71\t\n72\t- No TUI. Explicitly out of scope (user: \"don't do tui\"). Marvin's\n73\t  `investigate_tui.go` overview model is not being ported. Output is a\n74\t  printed turn-N banner + per-turn log file, with `--verbose` to tee\n75\t  stdout to the terminal.\n76\t- Not a wholesale port of marvin: only the investigate flow is in scope,\n77\t  not `marvin plan`, `marvin work`, `marvin wt`, `marvin clean`, or\n78\t  `marvin memory`. Marvin's `--brainstorm` editor flow is also out of\n79\t  scope for this PR — investigate launches straight into the loop.\n80\t- Not changing how `entire review` works, its settings schema, its storage\n81\t  format, or its checkpoint metadata layout. Investigate sits alongside\n82\t  review on the same scaffolding; review behavior is unchanged.\n83\t- Not introducing a new checkpoint storage primitive or branch.\n84\t  Investigations live in the existing `entire/checkpoints/v1` metadata\n85\t  with a new `Kind`, not a separate branch or store.\n86\t- Not building a generic web-fetch / scraping framework. `--issue-link`\n87\t  resolves GitHub issues and PRs through the `gh` CLI; non-GitHub URLs\n88\t  fail with a clear error directing the user to seed-doc instead.\n89\t- Not moving `entire review` under a `labs` namespace or otherwise\n90\t  changing its invocation path — `entire labs` remains a discovery\n91\t  command per the prior decision (#1130).\n92\t- Not extending `Kind.IsReview()` to cover investigate. Investigate gets\n93\t  its own `Kind.IsInvestigate()` predicate and its own `HasInvestigation`\n94\t  umbrella; the existing review umbrella keeps its narrow meaning.\n95\t- Not changing the remote `entire search` service or inventing a new\n96\t  search-side investigation badge/filter in this PR. Search may still match\n97\t  investigation content through whatever the existing backend indexes, but\n98\t  this plan does not depend on or promise new search-service behavior.\n99\t\n100\t## Proposal\n101\t\n102\t### 1. Command surface\n103\t\n104\t```\n105\tentire investigate                              # Run with config (or first-run picker)\n106\tentire investigate [seed-doc]                   # Use seed file as starting findings\n107\tentire investigate --topic \"<question>\"         # Or pass a topic directly\n108\tentire investigate --issue-link <github-url>    # Pull GH issue/PR body as seed\n109\tentire investigate --agents <csv>               # Override configured agents\n110\tentire investigate --max-turns N                # Per-agent turn budget (default: 3)\n111\tentire investigate --quorum N                   # Approvals required (default: all)\n112\tentire investigate --output <path>              # Override findings doc location\n113\tentire investigate --continue <run-id>          # Resume a paused/stalled run\n114\tentire investigate --edit                       # Re-open the config picker\n115\tentire investigate --findings                   # Browse local investigation manifests\n116\tentire investigate --verbose                    # Tee per-turn stdout to terminal\n117\t\n118\tentire investigate fix [<run-id>]               # Open a coding agent with findings as context\n119\tentire investigate attach <session-id>          # Tag an existing session as investigate (post-hoc)\n120\t```\n121\t\n122\tCobra placement: `investigate.NewCommand(buildInvestigateDeps(newInvestigateAttachCmd()))`\n123\tin `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`, parallel to how `cliReview.NewCommand(...)` is\n124\twired today for `entire review`. The command is `Hidden: true` (mirrors\n125\treview during the labs phase), and an `experimentalCommands` entry is added\n126\tin `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go` so `entire labs` lists it.\n127\t\n128\tValidation rules:\n129\t- At most one of `[seed-doc]`, `--topic`, `--issue-link` may be set per run.\n130\t- `--continue` is mutually exclusive with the seed/topic/issue inputs.\n131\t- Every selected agent must satisfy both constraints review already depends on:\n132\t  a non-interactive launcher/spawner exists, and Entire hooks are installed for\n133\t  that agent in the current repo. Config or `--agents` overrides that name an\n134\t  agent without hooks fail with the same style of actionable error as\n135\t  `entire review` (\"run `entire configure --agent <name>` first\").\n136\t- `fix` and `attach` are sibling subcommands of `investigate`, registered the\n137\t  same way `review attach` is wired today via `Deps.AttachCmd`.\n138\t\n139\t### 2. Settings schema\n140\t\n141\tAdd an `Investigate` field to `EntireSettings` in\n142\t`cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`:\n143\t\n144\t```json\n145\t{\n146\t  \"investigate\": {\n147\t    \"agents\": [\"claude-code\", \"codex\"],\n148\t    \"max_turns\": 3,\n149\t    \"quorum\": 0,\n150\t    \"always_prompt\": \"Be skeptical and cite line numbers.\"\n151\t  }\n152\t}\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\tDiffers from `Review` by design: review configures *per-agent skill lists*\n156\tbecause each agent runs different skills; investigate runs the same shared\n157\tinvestigate prompt across all agents, so per-agent customization adds no\n158\tvalue and `agents` is a flat list. `quorum: 0` means \"all agents must\n159\tapprove\" (matches marvin). `always_prompt` is appended to every turn's\n160\tprompt, parallel to `ReviewConfig.Prompt`.\n161\t\n162\tFirst-run setup: `runInvestigateConfigPicker` shows a multi-select of agents\n163\tthat satisfy two predicates in the current repo: (1) a `Spawner` is\n164\tregistered for the agent (today: claude-code, codex, gemini-cli — the same\n165\tthree agents that already have `buildReviewCmd` helpers and reviewer.go\n166\tfiles), AND (2) `agent.Get(name).AreHooksInstalled(ctx)` returns true.\n167\tNon-spawnable agents (cursor, opencode, factoryai-droid, copilot-cli) and\n168\ttest-only agents (vogon) are filtered out at predicate (1). Agents without\n169\thooks are excluded at predicate (2) because investigate's value proposition\n170\tis automatic session tagging via `UserPromptSubmit` plus later condensation,\n171\tnot a best-effort transcript scrape.\n172\t\n173\t### 3. Storage layout\n174\t\n175\tFindings doc + timeline (in worktree, optionally committed by the user):\n176\t\n177\t```\n178\t.entire/investigations/<slug>.md            # Findings doc\n179\t.entire/investigations/<slug>-timeline.md   # Per-turn timeline with stances\n180\t```\n181\t\n182\tPer-run state and transcripts (under git common dir, never committed,\n183\tper-worktree-safe by living next to `.git/entire-sessions/`):\n184\t\n185\t```\n186\t.git/entire-investigations/state/<run-id>.json          # Round, turn count, stances\n187\t.git/entire-investigations/transcripts/<run-id>/\n188\t  turn-1-claude-code.log\n189\t  turn-2-codex.log\n190\t  ...\n191\t.git/entire-investigations/manifests/<timestamp>-<run-id>.json   # For --findings browsing\n192\t```\n193\t\n194\t`<slug>` is `slugifyTopic(topic)` (port the helper from\n195\t`marvin/internal/cli/plan.go`). `<run-id>` is a 12-hex random ID generated at\n196\tloop start and embedded in env vars so all per-turn agent sessions can be\n197\tcorrelated.\n198\t\n199\tBootstrap behavior should mirror marvin's setup path rather than inventing a\n200\tnew document contract. If the user passed `[seed-doc]`, copy it verbatim into\n201\tthe findings doc and derive the topic from `# Investigation: ...`, then the\n202\tfirst markdown H1, then the filename as a last resort. If no seed doc was\n203\tpassed, render a scaffold with the same sections marvin uses today (`TLDR`,\n204\t`Question`, `Prior work`, `System under investigation`, `Approach`,\n205\t`Findings`, `Unknowns / Assumptions`, `Conclusion`) and pre-fill a\n206\t`## Prior Entire Context` block by running the current Entire-history lookup\n207\tflow (`entire search \"<topic>\" --json --limit 3 --repo \"*\"` plus short\n208\tcheckpoint explain excerpts for returned hits). `--issue-link` should\n209\tgenerate a scaffold-compatible seed doc instead of a one-off markdown shape so\n210\tthe first agent turn starts from the same document structure as every other\n211\tinvestigation run.\n212\t\n213\tPer-session state and condensation reuse the existing pipeline unchanged:\n214\t\n215\t- `.git/entire-sessions/<session-id>.json` stores `Kind = \"agent_investigate\"`,\n216\t  `InvestigatePrompt`, plus three new fields: `InvestigateRunID`,\n217\t  `InvestigateRound`, `InvestigateTurn`, `InvestigateAgent`.\n218\t- On the next user commit, the existing PostCommit condense path copies the\n219\t  session into `entire/checkpoints/v1` with `Kind` and `ReviewSkills`-style\n220\t  metadata fields propagated. Multi-session checkpoint format already supports\n221\t  multiple sessions per checkpoint; each turn's session lands in its own\n222\t  numbered subfolder (`0/`, `1/`, ...).\n223\t\n224\t### 4. Env-var handshake\n225\t\n226\tParallel package `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/env.go`:\n227\t\n228\t```go\n229\tconst (\n230\t    EnvSession      = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_SESSION\"      // \"1\"\n231\t    EnvAgent        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_AGENT\"        // \"claude-code\"\n232\t    EnvRunID        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_RUN_ID\"       // 12-hex\n233\t    EnvRound        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_ROUND\"        // \"1\", \"2\", ...\n234\t    EnvTurn         = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TURN\"         // overall turn index\n235\t    EnvTopic        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TOPIC\"        // human-readable topic\n236\t    EnvPrompt       = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_PROMPT\"       // composed prompt\n237\t    EnvFindingsDoc  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_FINDINGS_DOC\" // absolute path\n238\t    EnvTimelineDoc  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TIMELINE_DOC\" // absolute path\n239\t    EnvStartingSHA  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_STARTING_SHA\" // anti-stale-env guard\n240\t)\n241\t```\n242\t\n243\t`AppendInvestigateEnv` mirrors `review.AppendReviewEnv`: strips any existing\n244\t`ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` entries from `base`, then appends the contract\n245\tvariables. Each spawned process inherits its own copy, so concurrent\n246\tworktrees and concurrent investigations cannot leak env into each other.\n247\t\n248\t### 5. Loop architecture\n249\t\n250\tPort marvin's `runPlanLoop` into `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/loop.go`,\n251\tspecialised to the investigate mode:\n252\t\n253\t```go\n254\tfunc runInvestigateLoop(ctx context.Context, deps LoopDeps) (Result, error)\n255\t```\n256\t\n257\tPer-turn flow:\n258\t1. Hash findings doc + timeline before the turn and again after the turn, and\n259\t   persist `PlanChanged` / `TimelineChanged`-style booleans in run state and\n260\t   manifests for operator visibility. Mirror marvin's current bookkeeping here\n261\t   instead of inventing extra control flow around \"no edit\" turns.\n262\t2. Resolve the agent's spawner via `deps.SpawnerFor(agentName)` — this is\n263\t   the new shared interface (see §6) that returns an `*exec.Cmd` builder.\n264\t3. Compose the per-turn prompt via `ComposeInvestigatePrompt(in)` (port of\n265\t   marvin's `buildInvestigatePrompt`, including the shared prior-decisions /\n266\t   prior-claims / prior-fixes / memory-tools preamble plus the\n267\t   investigate-specific body, with `Files: { Findings, Timeline }` pointing\n268\t   at the worktree paths).\n269\t4. Spawn the agent with `cmd.Stdout = MultiWriter(perTurnLogFile, optionalTeeStdout)`.\n270\t5. After exit, parse the timeline file for the new `## Turn N — <agent>`\n271\t   entry, read the `**Stance:**` line, and record it in run state. If the\n272\t   header or stance line is missing/unparseable, record `unknown` and warn,\n273\t   matching marvin's current parser behavior rather than synthesizing a fake\n274\t   `request-changes` vote.\n275\t6. Persist run state to `.git/entire-investigations/state/<run-id>.json` after\n276\t   every turn so `--continue` can resume.\n277\t\n278\tLoop termination:\n279\t- Quorum reached when the count of `approve` stances in the most recent\n280\t  fully-played round is ≥ `quorum` (default `len(agents)`).\n281\t- `paused` when ctx is cancelled (Ctrl+C) or an agent fails twice in a row.\n282\t- `stalled` when `max-turns * len(agents)` turns have been played without\n283\t  quorum.\n284\t\n285\tThe loop is single-threaded by design — each turn waits for the previous\n286\tagent to exit before starting the next. This is the correct shape for\n287\tinvestigate: agents must read each other's edits to make progress, so\n288\tparallelism would hurt.\n289\t\n290\t### 6. Shared agent spawner\n291\t\n292\tRefactor opportunity: `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go` already\n293\tencapsulates \"build *exec.Cmd from RunConfig\" via\n294\t`ReviewerTemplate.BuildCmd`. Extract a smaller `Spawner` interface to\n295\t`cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/` so both review and investigate consume it:\n296\t\n297\t```go\n298\ttype Spawner interface {\n299\t    Name() string\n300\t    // BuildCmd returns a non-started exec.Cmd. The caller passes the\n301\t    // composed env (already including ENTIRE_REVIEW_* or ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*\n302\t    // produced by review.AppendReviewEnv / investigate.AppendInvestigateEnv)\n303\t    // and the composed prompt. Spawner stays env-contract-agnostic.\n304\t    BuildCmd(ctx context.Context, env []string, prompt string) *exec.Cmd\n305\t}\n306\t```\n307\t\n308\tPer-agent implementations live in each agent's package\n309\t(`agent/claudecode/spawner.go`, `agent/codex/spawner.go`,\n310\t`agent/geminicli/spawner.go`) and are tiny — the existing `buildReviewCmd`\n311\tbodies (argv shape + stdin wiring) move here, with `AppendReviewEnv`\n312\tfactored out to the caller. Review wraps a `Spawner` inside its existing\n313\tparser-driven `ReviewerTemplate` (BuildCmd now reads `cfg.Prompt =\n314\tComposeReviewPrompt(cfg)` then `env := AppendReviewEnv(os.Environ(),\n315\tagentName, cfg, prompt); spawner.BuildCmd(ctx, env, prompt)`); investigate\n316\twraps the same `Spawner` with a log-file-piping driver and\n317\t`AppendInvestigateEnv` instead. Review's existing argv contract tests\n318\t(`agent/<name>/reviewer_test.go`) move to the spawner package and are\n319\tre-pointed at the new helper, preserving the regression net.\n320\t\n321\tDo not reuse `agent.LauncherFor` for this path. The existing `LaunchCmd`\n322\timplementations in `agent/claudecode/claude.go`, `agent/codex/codex.go`, and\n323\t`agent/geminicli/gemini.go` are foreground TTY-oriented entrypoints\n324\t(`claude <prompt>`, `codex <prompt>`, `gemini <prompt>`) intended for normal\n325\tinteractive coding sessions and `review --fix`, not for a headless loop that\n326\tmust inject `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*`, capture deterministic stdout, and return\n327\twithout user keystrokes. Investigate needs the review-style non-interactive\n328\tbuilders, not the interactive launcher contract.\n329\t\n330\tThis is a small refactor (≈ 60 LOC moved across three files) and is\n331\tincluded in this PR because investigate cannot ship without a way to\n332\texec each agent non-interactively, and duplicating the argv constructors\n333\twould create the kind of drift the env-var contract is designed to prevent.\n334\t\n335\t### 7. Lifecycle adoption\n336\t\n337\tAdd `adoptInvestigateEnv(ctx, state, expectedAgent)` next to\n338\t`adoptReviewEnv` in `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`. Same shape: short-circuit\n339\tif state.Kind already set; check `EnvSession == \"1\"`; verify `EnvAgent` and\n340\t`EnvStartingSHA` match; tag state.\n341\t\n342\t```go\n343\tstate.Kind = session.KindAgentInvestigate\n344\tstate.InvestigateRunID = os.Getenv(investigate.EnvRunID)\n345\tstate.InvestigateRound = atoiOrZero(os.Getenv(investigate.EnvRound))\n346\tstate.InvestigateTurn = atoiOrZero(os.Getenv(investigate.EnvTurn))\n347\tstate.InvestigateTopic = os.Getenv(investigate.EnvTopic)\n348\tstate.InvestigatePrompt = os.Getenv(investigate.EnvPrompt)\n349\t```\n350\t\n351\tAdoption fires from the same `InitializeSession` site that calls\n352\t`adoptReviewEnv` today, immediately after. `Kind` is single-valued, so a\n353\tsession is either a review OR an investigate, never both.\n354\t\n355\t### 8. Checkpoint metadata changes\n356\t\n357\t`cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`:\n358\t- New const `KindAgentInvestigate Kind = \"agent_investigate\"`.\n359\t- New method `Kind.IsInvestigate() bool { return k == KindAgentInvestigate }`.\n360\t- New `State` fields: `InvestigateRunID`, `InvestigateRound`, `InvestigateTurn`,\n361\t  `InvestigateTopic`, `InvestigatePrompt` (all `omitempty`).\n362\t\n363\t`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go`:\n364\t- New `CommittedMetadata` fields parallel to `ReviewSkills` / `ReviewPrompt`:\n365\t  `InvestigateRunID`, `InvestigateRound`, `InvestigateTurn`,\n366\t  `InvestigateTopic`, `InvestigatePrompt`.\n367\t- New `CheckpointSummary` field: `HasInvestigation bool` with `omitempty`.\n368\t- Caller-side flag (matching `HasReview`): a new field\n369\t  `WriteCommittedOptions.HasInvestigation` that the PostCommit dispatcher\n370\t  computes via `state.Kind.IsInvestigate()` and propagates into the summary\n371\t  the same way `HasReview` flows today.\n372\t\n373\t`committed.go`'s `WriteCommitted` propagates `HasInvestigation` with the\n374\texisting OR-style merge that protects `HasReview`: if a prior session in\n375\tthis checkpoint already set the flag, keep it set.\n376\t\n377\tLocal readers must be updated explicitly; they do not \"just work\" today:\n378\t\n379\t- `cmd/entire/cli/status.go` currently only consults `headHasReviewCheckpoint`.\n380\t  Replace that single-purpose helper with a generic HEAD checkpoint summary\n381\t  lookup (or parallel helpers backed by one lookup) so status can print\n382\t  `Review` and `Investigation` lines independently when HEAD's checkpoint\n383\t  summary carries either umbrella flag.\n384\t- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go` currently exposes `has_review` at the\n385\t  top level and only review-specific session fields in its JSON envelope.\n386\t  Add `has_investigation` plus session-level\n387\t  `investigate_run_id`, `investigate_round`, `investigate_turn`, and\n388\t  `investigate_topic` fields so `entire checkpoint explain --json` can show\n389\t  the new metadata without requiring transcript reads.\n390\t- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go` can keep `InvestigatePrompt` out of the\n391\t  JSON envelope, matching the current review export shape: prompt bodies are\n392\t  available through transcript/prompt files when explicitly requested, but the\n393\t  metadata export stays compact.\n394\t\n395\tBackwards compat: `omitempty` JSON tag means old metadata is read with\n396\tzero values; old CLIs reading new metadata see `Kind = \"agent_investigate\"`\n397\tas an unknown string and treat the session as \"normal\" — no review\n398\tbehaviour fires, which is the correct fallback.\n399\t\n400\t`entire search` is intentionally not changed here. Its CLI surface talks to a\n401\tremote search service with its own schema and ranking behavior; this PR only\n402\tguarantees the local checkpoint metadata and manifests are present for future\n403\tindexing, not that the cloud service grows an investigation-aware badge or\n404\tfilter in lockstep.\n405\t\n406\t### 9. `--issue-link` semantics\n407\t\n408\tImplementation in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/issuelink.go`:\n409\t\n410\t```go\n411\tfunc ResolveIssueLink(ctx context.Context, url string) (seedDoc []byte, topic string, err error)\n412\t```\n413\t\n414\t1. Parse URL. If host is `github.com` and path matches\n415\t   `/<owner>/<repo>/(issues|pull)/<n>`, dispatch to `gh issue view` or\n416\t   `gh pr view` with `--json title,body,author,createdAt,labels,comments`.\n417\t   Compose a markdown seed doc:\n418\t\n419\t   ```\n420\t   # Investigation: <title>\n421\t\n422\t   **Source:** <url>\n423\t   **Author:** @<author>\n424\t   **Created:** <createdAt>\n425\t   **Labels:** <labels>\n426\t\n427\t   ## Question\n428\t\n429\t   <body>\n430\t\n431\t   ## Comments\n432\t\n433\t   - **@<commenter> (<createdAt>):** <comment-body>\n434\t   ...\n435\t   ```\n436\t\n437\t2. If host is `github.com` but path doesn't match, return a clear error\n438\t   pointing the user at `--topic` or seeding from a file.\n439\t3. If host is anything else, return:\n440\t   `\"--issue-link only supports GitHub issues and PRs in this release;\n441\t    save the issue body to a file and pass it as a positional [seed-doc]\"`.\n442\t4. If `gh` is not on PATH, return a clear error: `\"--issue-link requires\n443\t    the gh CLI; install it (https://cli.github.com) or pass [seed-doc]\"`.\n444\t\n445\tThe `gh` invocation is wrapped in a `runGhFn` package var so unit tests can\n446\tinject a fake. No HTTP client, no scraping, no auth handling — `gh` already\n447\towns auth and is the standard Entire users have.\n448\t\n449\tTopic derivation: prefer the issue/PR title; fall back to the URL itself if\n450\tempty. The composed seed doc is written to `<findings-doc-path>` and the\n451\tloop runs against it.\n452\t\n453\t### 10. `entire investigate fix` semantics\n454\t\n455\tMirrors `entire review --fix`. Resolves a manifest by `<run-id>` (or prompts\n456\tto pick the most recent). Composes a follow-up prompt like:\n457\t\n458\t> A prior multi-agent investigation produced these findings. Use them as\n459\t> grounded context to plan the next step. Do not re-investigate the same\n460\t> question — assume the findings are correct unless you find direct\n461\t> evidence to the contrary.\n462\t>\n463\t> ## Investigation findings\n464\t>\n465\t> <body of `.entire/investigations/<slug>.md`>\n466\t>\n467\t> ## Investigation timeline\n468\t>\n469\t> <body of `.entire/investigations/<slug>-timeline.md`>\n470\t\n471\tThen launches a normal `entire`-aware coding agent session via the existing\n472\t`launchReviewFixAgent` helper, which is renamed `launchFixAgent` and moved\n473\tfrom `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go` to a new `cmd/entire/cli/agentlaunch/`\n474\tpackage so both review-fix and investigate-fix can call it. The helper's\n475\tenv-stripping step is broadened from `withoutReviewEnv` to also strip\n476\t`ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` entries before exec, so a fix session never inherits\n477\teither set of provenance env vars from its parent. The launched session is\n478\ta plain coding session, not tagged as review or investigate.\n479\t\n480\tThis is \"the way to feed a saved investigation back into a follow-up agent\n481\trun for context\" called for in the goals.\n482\t\n483\t### 11. Picker / first-run setup\n484\t\n485\t`runInvestigateConfigPicker` in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/picker.go`:\n486\t\n487\t- Lists agents that are both launchable and hook-installed in the current\n488\t  repo (filters via `SpawnerFor != nil` plus the same hook-installed check\n489\t  review uses).\n490\t- Multi-select — needs at least one selection.\n491\t- Asks for max-turns (default 3) and quorum (default 0 = all).\n492\t- Saves to `EntireSettings.Investigate`.\n493\t\n494\t`ConfirmFirstRunSetup` mirrors review's: when `entire investigate` runs with\n495\tno config, print a banner explaining that we're configuring before running,\n496\tget y/N confirmation, run the picker, then drop into the loop.\n497\t\n498\t### 12. Backwards compat / migrations\n499\t\n500\t- New JSON fields all carry `omitempty`; old metadata reads with zero values.\n501\t- `Kind` is a string; the new `\"agent_investigate\"` value is ignored by old\n502\t  CLIs, which treat the session as untagged (normal).\n503\t- No file format migrations. No state-file rewrites. No\n504\t  `entire/checkpoints/v1` rewrites.\n505\t- The shared-spawner refactor (§6) preserves identical argv for review;\n506\t  contract tests pin the exact argv per agent so we'd catch any drift in CI.\n507\t\n508\t### 13. Telemetry / logging\n509\t\n510\t- All logging uses the existing `logging` package with structured slog\n511\t  attrs (`event`, `agent`, `round`, `turn`, `run_id`, `outcome`).\n512\t- No external telemetry transports added. The existing\n513\t  `__send_analytics` path picks up the new event names via its lowercase\n514\t  command-name prefix without any code change in the analytics sender.\n515\t- Privacy: per CLAUDE.md, we never log prompts, file bodies, or commit\n516\t  messages — only operational metadata (counts, IDs, paths, durations).\n517\t\n518\t### 14. Testing strategy\n519\t\n520\tAll in this PR.\n521\t\n522\t**Unit tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/`:\n523\t- `prompt_test.go`: golden-file tests for `ComposeInvestigatePrompt` covering\n524\t  first round, mid-loop turn, with/without `always_prompt`, with prior\n525\t  reviewer comments, and with prior decisions / claims / fixes so the shared\n526\t  prompt preamble is pinned alongside the investigate body.\n527\t- `bootstrap_test.go`: seed-doc passthrough, scaffold rendering with\n528\t  `## Prior Entire Context`, and topic derivation from `# Investigation:`,\n529\t  first H1, then filename fallback.\n530\t- `env_test.go`: `EncodeXxx` / `DecodeXxx` round-trips, `AppendInvestigateEnv`\n531\t  strips stale entries, `isInvestigateEnvEntry` true/false table.\n532\t- `issuelink_test.go`: URL parsing table (issue vs PR vs unsupported host\n533\t  vs malformed), fake-`gh` injection produces expected seed-doc body, error\n534\t  paths surface actionable messages.\n535\t- `loop_test.go`: `runInvestigateLoop` with a fake spawner that produces\n536\t  scripted timeline edits per turn — verifies quorum detection, max-turns\n537\t  termination, paused-on-second-failure, `unknown` stance fallback,\n538\t  changed-file booleans, and resume from state file.\n539\t- `parse_stance_test.go`: scans timeline for `**Stance:**` lines, tolerant\n540\t  of whitespace and mixed dash separators in headings.\n541\t\n542\t**Lifecycle tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`:\n543\t- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_Success` — env vars set, state tagged.\n544\t- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_AgentMismatch` — env from a different agent does\n545\t  not tag the session.\n546\t- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_StaleStartingSHA` — base-commit guard.\n547\t- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_AlreadyTaggedNotOverwritten` — review session is\n548\t  not silently re-kinded.\n549\t\n550\t**Checkpoint tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`:\n551\t- `TestCommittedMetadata_AgentInvestigate` — JSON wire-format pin.\n552\t- `TestCheckpointSummary_HasInvestigation` — JSON wire-format pin including\n553\t  `omitempty` zero-value behaviour, mirroring `TestCheckpointSummary_HasReview`.\n554\t\n555\t**Spawner refactor regression tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/`:\n556\t- `TestClaudeCodeSpawner_ArgvUnchanged`,\n557\t  `TestCodexSpawner_ArgvUnchanged`,\n558\t  `TestGeminiCLISpawner_ArgvUnchanged` — golden-file pins of the exact argv\n559\t  produced for each agent given a fixed prompt and env, so review's pre-refactor\n560\t  argv stays byte-identical post-refactor. These pins replace the existing\n561\t  `agent/<name>/reviewer_test.go` argv assertions.\n562\t\n563\t**Reader / UX tests**:\n564\t- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export_test.go`: pins the new\n565\t  `has_investigation`, `investigate_run_id`, `investigate_round`,\n566\t  `investigate_turn`, and `investigate_topic` JSON fields and their\n567\t  `omitempty` behavior.\n568\t- `cmd/entire/cli/status_test.go` (or the generalized HEAD-checkpoint helper\n569\t  tests if that logic moves out of `status.go`): verifies status prints the\n570\t  new `Investigation · investigated (checkpoint <id>)` line, and that review +\n571\t  investigation can coexist in the rendered status output without one hiding\n572\t  the other.\n573\t- `cmd/entire/cli/attach_test.go`: extends the existing review-attach surface\n574\t  coverage with investigate tagging through the generalized attach path.\n575\t\n576\t**Integration tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`:\n577\t- `TestInvestigate_EnvVarAdoptionCondensesMetadataOnNextCommit` — modeled on\n578\t  `integration_test/review_test.go`: set `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` on a simulated\n579\t  hook event, assert the session state is tagged as investigate, then commit\n580\t  and verify `HasInvestigation` plus the investigate metadata fields on the\n581\t  checkpoint.\n582\t- `TestInvestigateCommand_PassesInvestigateEnvToSpawnedAgentHooks` — also\n583\t  modeled on the review integration path, but with fake `claude` / `codex`\n584\t  binaries on `PATH`. Each fake binary appends one turn entry to the\n585\t  findings/timeline files, calls `\"$ENTIRE_TEST_BINARY\" hooks <agent>\n586\t  user-prompt-submit`, then exits 0. This verifies the real cobra command,\n587\t  spawner wiring, and env-var handshake without any API calls.\n588\t- `TestInvestigateAttach_TagsAttachedSessionAsInvestigate` — attaches a saved\n589\t  transcript post-hoc and asserts the checkpoint/session metadata records\n590\t  `Kind = agent_investigate`.\n591\t- `TestInvestigate_Continue_Resumes` — seed a run-state file plus findings and\n592\t  timeline docs, then resume with fake spawned agents and verify the next\n593\t  expected turn is played instead of replaying completed turns.\n594\t- `TestInvestigate_IssueLink_GhFake` — fake `gh` binary on PATH returns a\n595\t  fixture issue body; verify seed doc bootstrap.\n596\t\n597\t**No new E2E canary in this PR.** Vogon is intentionally test-only,\n598\tnon-launchable, and `AreHooksInstalled()` returns false, so it cannot satisfy\n599\tthe same preflight path the real command will use. Real-agent E2E remains\n600\topt-in per repo policy; the product verification bar here is unit tests plus\n601\tthe fake-binary integration harness above.\n602\t\n603\t### 15. Files added / modified\n604\t\n605\tNew files (all under `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/`):\n606\t- `cmd.go` — cobra wiring, `NewCommand(deps)`, flag parsing.\n607\t- `loop.go` — `runInvestigateLoop`, per-turn driver, stance parsing.\n608\t- `prompt.go` — `ComposeInvestigatePrompt`.\n609\t- `env.go` — env var constants + helpers.\n610\t- `picker.go` — first-run config picker.\n611\t- `manifest.go` — local manifest read/write (mirrors review).\n612\t- `fix.go` — `entire investigate fix` subcommand.\n613\t- `attach.go` — `entire investigate attach <session-id>`.\n614\t- `findings.go` — `--findings` browser.\n615\t- `issuelink.go` — GitHub issue/PR resolver via `gh`.\n616\t- `state.go` — `RunState` JSON read/write.\n617\t- Plus matching `_test.go` files per §14.\n618\t\n619\tNew files under `cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/`:\n620\t- `spawn.go` — `Spawner` interface, registry helper.\n621\t- `spawner_test.go` — `Test<Agent>Spawner_ArgvUnchanged` golden-file pins.\n622\t- Per-agent: small additions to `agent/claudecode/spawner.go`,\n623\t  `agent/codex/spawner.go`, `agent/geminicli/spawner.go` (move existing\n624\t  `buildReviewCmd` argv construction here and parameterise by env).\n625\t\n626\tNew file `cmd/entire/cli/agentlaunch/launch.go`:\n627\t- `launchFixAgent(ctx, agentName, prompt) error` — moved from\n628\t  `review/fix.go:launchReviewFixAgent`, with env stripping broadened to\n629\t  cover both `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` and `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*`.\n630\t\n631\tModified existing files:\n632\t- `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go` — append `investigate` to `experimentalCommands`.\n633\t- `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` and a new `investigate_bridge.go` glue file —\n634\t  wire `investigate.NewCommand(...)` plus the CLI-package deps it needs.\n635\t- `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go` — call `adoptInvestigateEnv` next to\n636\t  `adoptReviewEnv`.\n637\t- `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go` — add `KindAgentInvestigate`,\n638\t  `Kind.IsInvestigate()`, new state fields.\n639\t- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go` — add `HasInvestigation`,\n640\t  investigate metadata fields.\n641\t- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` — propagate `HasInvestigation`.\n642\t- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go` — surface investigate fields in JSON\n643\t  export.\n644\t- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` — add `Investigate` field +\n645\t  helper accessors.\n646\t- `cmd/entire/cli/status.go` and the helper that reads HEAD checkpoint\n647\t  summary flags — surface investigation state next to review state.\n648\t- `cmd/entire/cli/attach.go` — generalize the attach path so investigate\n649\t  attach can tag a session and write investigate metadata.\n650\t- `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go` and the per-agent\n651\t  `reviewer.go` files — wrap the new `Spawner` instead of inlining argv.\n652\t- `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go` — call into\n653\t  `agentlaunch.launchFixAgent` instead of the local\n654\t  `launchReviewFixAgent`; remove the now-shared body.\n655\t- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/investigate_test.go` — fake-binary\n656\t  command/integration coverage for the new loop.\n657\t- `CLAUDE.md` — append an `entire investigate` section parallel to\n658\t  `entire review`.\n659\t\n660\tApproximate diff size: ~1,700 lines added (≈ 1,100 product, ≈ 600 tests),\n661\t~200 lines moved/refactored for the spawner extraction, the\n662\t`launchReviewFixAgent` → `agentlaunch.launchFixAgent` move, and the\n663\tHEAD-checkpoint helper generalization. One PR.\n664\t\n665\t## Alternatives Considered\n666\t\n667\t**1. Run agents in parallel (not round-robin).** Rejected. Agents must read\n668\teach other's findings to converge; parallel runs would either produce\n669\tnon-overlapping findings (no convergence) or require a merge step that\n670\tre-introduces sequential editing. Marvin chose round-robin for the same\n671\treason.\n672\t\n673\t**2. Store findings in `~/.entire/investigations/` like marvin does in\n674\t`~/.marvin/`.** Rejected. Entire is per-repo and ties context to\n675\tcheckpoints; a per-repo path under `.entire/` (worktree) and\n676\t`.git/entire-investigations/` (state) keeps everything addressable from the\n677\trepo and survives the same way checkpoints do. Marvin's global home was\n678\tappropriate for a multi-repo POC; entire's model is repo-scoped.\n679\t\n680\t**3. Reuse `Kind = \"agent_review\"` and extend `IsReview()` to cover\n681\tinvestigate, with a new sub-discriminator.** Rejected. Review and\n682\tinvestigate produce different artifacts (skills output vs findings doc),\n683\thave different commit-time UX (re-run guard wording, status banner), and\n684\tthe existing `HasReview` docstring explicitly says it's the umbrella for\n685\t\"any review happened\". Conflating the two breaks the umbrella's meaning\n686\tand forces every downstream reader to disambiguate. A parallel\n687\t`HasInvestigation` flag is simpler.\n688\t\n689\t**4. Build a generic web fetcher behind `--issue-link`.** Rejected per\n690\tnon-goals. `gh` already handles GitHub auth, rate limits, and JSON output;\n691\tnon-GitHub hosts (Linear, GitLab, Jira) need different auth models and\n692\tresponse shapes that do not generalise. A pluggable fetcher framework is\n693\treal engineering and not something we can afford to ship correctly inside\n694\tthis PR. Users with non-GitHub sources can pre-paste content into a seed\n695\tfile in two seconds.\n696\t\n697\t**5. Live overview TUI like marvin's `investigate_tui.go`.** Rejected per\n698\tthe user's explicit \"don't do tui\". The non-TUI design also unblocks\n699\trunning investigate inside another agent session (e.g. a Claude Code\n700\tsession calling `entire investigate` via Bash) — TUI sinks block on\n701\tkeypresses that never arrive in that context. Per-turn log files are\n702\tgreppable, archivable, and visible without ANSI gymnastics.\n703\t\n704\t**6. Skip the spawner refactor; duplicate argv builders for investigate.**\n705\tRejected. Three agents × two callers (review + investigate) = six places\n706\twhere argv must stay aligned. The next agent-flag tweak (e.g. a future\n707\t`--permission-mode` change) would silently drift across callers. Sharing\n708\tthrough a small `Spawner` interface costs ≈ 60 LOC and prevents the drift.\n709\t\n710\t## Risks & Mitigations\n711\t\n712\t- **Risk: `gh` not installed.** Detected at `--issue-link` resolution time;\n713\t  surface a clear error pointing at the `gh` install URL and the seed-doc\n714\t  fallback. Not blocking for the rest of the command.\n715\t- **Risk: agent fails to modify the findings doc.** The pre-turn hash check\n716\t  still detects \"no edit\", but the loop should surface that as bookkeeping\n717\t  (`PlanChanged=false` / `TimelineChanged=false`) plus an `unknown` stance\n718\t  warning when the timeline entry is missing, rather than inventing a vote the\n719\t  agent never cast. This keeps the control flow aligned with marvin's current\n720\t  behavior while still making silent turns obvious in logs and manifests.\n721\t- **Risk: stale `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` env from a parent shell tagging the\n722\t  wrong session.** Same protection as review: `EnvAgent` must match the\n723\t  hook's agent and `EnvStartingSHA` must match the session's base commit.\n724\t  Both must hold for adoption to fire; either mismatch leaves the session\n725\t  untagged with a logged warning.\n726\t- **Risk: the shared spawner refactor regresses review argv.** Contract\n727\t  tests in `agent/<name>/spawner_test.go` pin the exact argv string per\n728\t  agent; review's existing argv tests (e.g. `claudecode/reviewer_test.go`)\n729\t  also serve as a regression net via the wrapper.\n730\t- **Risk: investigation findings doc lands in the user's commit\n731\t  unintentionally.** Entire does not guarantee `.entire/` is ignored in every\n732\t  repo, and this repo's tracked `.gitignore` does not ignore it today. The\n733\t  findings doc is still a deliberate deliverable, so we do not auto-add a\n734\t  gitignore entry or auto-stage it; we surface the file path on completion so\n735\t  users can choose whether to commit it or ignore `.entire/investigations/`\n736\t  explicitly in their own repo.\n737\t- **Risk: `entire investigate` invoked from inside an existing agent\n738\t  session (Claude Code calling Bash → entire investigate).** Works by\n739\t  design — no TUI, env per process — but the inner sessions inherit\n740\t  `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` if the outer was a review. The\n741\t  `withoutReviewEnv`-style strip in `AppendInvestigateEnv` removes any\n742\t  `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` entries before appending investigate vars to prevent\n743\t  cross-tagging.\n744\t- **Risk: product plan overpromises cloud search behavior that this repo\n745\t  cannot ship.** Mitigation: scope the PR to local checkpoint/manifests UX\n746\t  only (`status`, `checkpoint explain`, `--findings`, `fix`) and document\n747\t  that dedicated `entire search` investigation surfacing depends on the\n748\t  remote service, so it is not part of this change set.\n749\t\n750\t## Decision\n751\t\n752\tApproved direction: ship as a single PR titled `feat(investigate): add\n753\tentire investigate command (labs)`. Includes the cobra command, the loop\n754\tdriver, the env-var contract, the lifecycle adoption, the\n755\t`HasInvestigation` summary flag, the status / explain-export surfacing, the\n756\tshared spawner refactor, the `--issue-link` resolver, the `fix` and\n757\t`attach` subcommands, the picker, the manifest reader, the fake-binary\n758\tintegration coverage, and the CLAUDE.md update.\n759\t\n760\tReviewer focus areas:\n761\t- Env-var contract correctness (multi-tenant inheritance, stale-env\n762\t  protection).\n763\t- Lifecycle adoption ordering vs `adoptReviewEnv`.\n764\t- Checkpoint metadata back-compat (old CLI reading new metadata).\n765\t- Spawner refactor preserves exact argv per agent.\n766\t- `--issue-link` URL parsing rejects malformed inputs.\n767\t"}]},"uuid":"56ba8a39-05de-4b2b-82d7-cf363680e4e2","timestamp":"2026-05-09T00:04:00.451Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/plans/entire-labs-investigate/prompt.md","content":"# Plan: prompt\n\n**Status:** drafting\n**Authors:** claude-code, codex\n**Created:** 2026-05-08\n\n## TLDR\n\nShip `entire investigate` as a hidden top-level command surfaced through\n`entire labs`. It runs a non-TUI marvin-style round-robin loop across\nlaunchable, hook-enabled agents (claude-code, codex, gemini-cli), bootstraps\na findings doc + timeline (including prior Entire context when there is no\nseed doc), and tags each spawned session with a new `agent_investigate` Kind\nso the next commit condenses the investigation into `entire/checkpoints/v1`\nalongside `entire review` runs. GitHub issue/PR URLs seed the loop through\n`gh`; a local manifest plus an `entire investigate fix` helper lets users feed\naccepted findings into a follow-up coding session. Biggest tradeoff:\ninvestigate gets its own `HasInvestigation` umbrella flag and\n`Kind.IsInvestigate()` predicate rather than reusing review's umbrella, so the\nfeature stays semantically honest at the cost of updating every local reader\nthat currently only knows about review.\n\n## Problem / Motivation\n\n`marvin investigate` (POC at `/Users/alisha/Projects/marvin`) runs a\nmulti-agent investigation against a seeded question or doc and produces a\nfindings + timeline artifact. We want to graduate that workflow into the\nEntire CLI as a real, supported command — `entire investigate` — that reuses\nthe `entire review` scaffolding so investigations are saved, linked to\ncheckpoints, and condensed onto `entire/checkpoints/v1` the same way reviews\nare. Today nothing in `entire` captures pre-implementation investigation\nwork; ad-hoc agent runs lose their context on the next commit, and there is\nno provenance trail tying \"we investigated X\" to the commit it informed.\n\nInvestigations also need to be triggerable from external work tracking. The\nuser should be able to point the command at a GitHub issue or PR (or any\ncode-issue link) and have it pull the linked content as the seed, without\nhand-copying the issue body into a doc.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Add a new `entire investigate` command that mirrors `entire review`'s\n  placement: top-level command, listed under `entire labs` as experimental,\n  invoked directly (no `entire labs investigate` namespace).\n- Reuse `entire review` scaffolding for persistence and provenance: an\n  `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` env-var handshake parallel to `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*`,\n  lifecycle adoption to tag the session, an `attach` subcommand,\n  condensation onto `entire/checkpoints/v1` via the existing multi-session\n  checkpoint format, and a new `HasInvestigation` umbrella flag on\n  `CheckpointSummary`.\n- Match the `marvin investigate` UX where it makes sense: accept either a\n  `--topic` (matching marvin's `--question`) or a `[seed-doc]` positional\n  path, port marvin's investigate prompt body verbatim, drive a round-robin\n  loop with stances and quorum, and persist a findings doc + timeline.\n- Add a `--issue-link <url>` flag that accepts GitHub issue and PR URLs\n  (resolved via `gh issue|pr view --json`), turns the issue body into a\n  seed findings doc, and falls back with a clear \"save to a file and pass\n  as a positional `[seed-doc]`\" error for unsupported hosts.\n- Provide a way to feed a saved investigation back into a follow-up agent\n  run: `entire investigate fix [<run-id>]` mirrors `entire review --fix` —\n  resolves the manifest, composes a prompt that says \"use these findings\n  as context, do not re-investigate\", and launches a regular coding agent\n  session.\n- Persist the findings as part of checkpoint metadata and local manifests so\n  `entire status`, `entire checkpoint explain --json`, and\n  `entire investigate --findings` / `fix` can surface them. Dedicated\n  `entire search` investigation UX is out of scope for this PR because it\n  depends on the cloud search service, not only this CLI repo.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No TUI. Explicitly out of scope (user: \"don't do tui\"). Marvin's\n  `investigate_tui.go` overview model is not being ported. Output is a\n  printed turn-N banner + per-turn log file, with `--verbose` to tee\n  stdout to the terminal.\n- Not a wholesale port of marvin: only the investigate flow is in scope,\n  not `marvin plan`, `marvin work`, `marvin wt`, `marvin clean`, or\n  `marvin memory`. Marvin's `--brainstorm` editor flow is also out of\n  scope for this PR — investigate launches straight into the loop.\n- Not changing how `entire review` works, its settings schema, its storage\n  format, or its checkpoint metadata layout. Investigate sits alongside\n  review on the same scaffolding; review behavior is unchanged.\n- Not introducing a new checkpoint storage primitive or branch.\n  Investigations live in the existing `entire/checkpoints/v1` metadata\n  with a new `Kind`, not a separate branch or store.\n- Not building a generic web-fetch / scraping framework. `--issue-link`\n  resolves GitHub issues and PRs through the `gh` CLI; non-GitHub URLs\n  fail with a clear error directing the user to seed-doc instead.\n- Not moving `entire review` under a `labs` namespace or otherwise\n  changing its invocation path — `entire labs` remains a discovery\n  command per the prior decision (#1130).\n- Not extending `Kind.IsReview()` to cover investigate. Investigate gets\n  its own `Kind.IsInvestigate()` predicate and its own `HasInvestigation`\n  umbrella; the existing review umbrella keeps its narrow meaning.\n- Not changing the remote `entire search` service or inventing a new\n  search-side investigation badge/filter in this PR. Search may still match\n  investigation content through whatever the existing backend indexes, but\n  this plan does not depend on or promise new search-service behavior.\n\n## Proposal\n\n### 1. Command surface\n\n```\nentire investigate                              # Run with config (or first-run picker)\nentire investigate [seed-doc]                   # Use seed file as starting findings\nentire investigate --topic \"<question>\"         # Or pass a topic directly\nentire investigate --issue-link <github-url>    # Pull GH issue/PR body as seed\nentire investigate --agents <csv>               # Override configured agents\nentire investigate --max-turns N                # Per-agent turn budget (default: 3)\nentire investigate --quorum N                   # Approvals required (default: all)\nentire investigate --output <path>              # Override findings doc location\nentire investigate --continue <run-id>          # Resume a paused/stalled run\nentire investigate --edit                       # Re-open the config picker\nentire investigate --findings                   # Browse local investigation manifests\nentire investigate --verbose                    # Tee per-turn stdout to terminal\n\nentire investigate fix [<run-id>]               # Open a coding agent with findings as context\nentire investigate attach <session-id>          # Tag an existing session as investigate (post-hoc)\n```\n\nCobra placement: `investigate.NewCommand(buildInvestigateDeps(newInvestigateAttachCmd()))`\nin `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`, parallel to how `cliReview.NewCommand(...)` is\nwired today for `entire review`. The command is `Hidden: true` (mirrors\nreview during the labs phase), and an `experimentalCommands` entry is added\nin `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go` so `entire labs` lists it.\n\nValidation rules:\n- At most one of `[seed-doc]`, `--topic`, `--issue-link` may be set per run.\n- `--continue` is mutually exclusive with the seed/topic/issue inputs.\n- Every selected agent must satisfy both constraints review already depends on:\n  a non-interactive launcher/spawner exists, and Entire hooks are installed for\n  that agent in the current repo. Config or `--agents` overrides that name an\n  agent without hooks fail with the same style of actionable error as\n  `entire review` (\"run `entire configure --agent <name>` first\").\n- `fix` and `attach` are sibling subcommands of `investigate`, registered the\n  same way `review attach` is wired today via `Deps.AttachCmd`.\n\n### 2. Settings schema\n\nAdd an `Investigate` field to `EntireSettings` in\n`cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"investigate\": {\n    \"agents\": [\"claude-code\", \"codex\"],\n    \"max_turns\": 3,\n    \"quorum\": 0,\n    \"always_prompt\": \"Be skeptical and cite line numbers.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDiffers from `Review` by design: review configures *per-agent skill lists*\nbecause each agent runs different skills; investigate runs the same shared\ninvestigate prompt across all agents, so per-agent customization adds no\nvalue and `agents` is a flat list. `quorum: 0` means \"all agents must\napprove\" (matches marvin). `always_prompt` is appended to every turn's\nprompt, parallel to `ReviewConfig.Prompt`.\n\nFirst-run setup: `runInvestigateConfigPicker` shows a multi-select of agents\nthat satisfy two predicates in the current repo: (1) a `Spawner` is\nregistered for the agent (today: claude-code, codex, gemini-cli — the same\nthree agents that already have `buildReviewCmd` helpers and reviewer.go\nfiles), AND (2) `agent.Get(name).AreHooksInstalled(ctx)` returns true.\nNon-spawnable agents (cursor, opencode, factoryai-droid, copilot-cli) and\ntest-only agents (vogon) are filtered out at predicate (1). Agents without\nhooks are excluded at predicate (2) because investigate's value proposition\nis automatic session tagging via `UserPromptSubmit` plus later condensation,\nnot a best-effort transcript scrape.\n\n### 3. Storage layout\n\nFindings doc + timeline (in worktree, optionally committed by the user):\n\n```\n.entire/investigations/<slug>.md            # Findings doc\n.entire/investigations/<slug>-timeline.md   # Per-turn timeline with stances\n```\n\nPer-run state and transcripts (under git common dir, never committed,\nper-worktree-safe by living next to `.git/entire-sessions/`):\n\n```\n.git/entire-investigations/state/<run-id>.json          # Round, turn count, stances\n.git/entire-investigations/transcripts/<run-id>/\n  turn-1-claude-code.log\n  turn-2-codex.log\n  ...\n.git/entire-investigations/manifests/<timestamp>-<run-id>.json   # For --findings browsing\n```\n\n`<slug>` is `slugifyTopic(topic)` (port the helper from\n`marvin/internal/cli/plan.go`). `<run-id>` is a 12-hex random ID generated at\nloop start and embedded in env vars so all per-turn agent sessions can be\ncorrelated.\n\nBootstrap behavior should mirror marvin's setup path rather than inventing a\nnew document contract. If the user passed `[seed-doc]`, copy it verbatim into\nthe findings doc and derive the topic from `# Investigation: ...`, then the\nfirst markdown H1, then the filename as a last resort. If no seed doc was\npassed, render a scaffold with the same sections marvin uses today (`TLDR`,\n`Question`, `Prior work`, `System under investigation`, `Approach`,\n`Findings`, `Unknowns / Assumptions`, `Conclusion`) and pre-fill a\n`## Prior Entire Context` block by running the current Entire-history lookup\nflow (`entire search \"<topic>\" --json --limit 3 --repo \"*\"` plus short\ncheckpoint explain excerpts for returned hits). `--issue-link` should\ngenerate a scaffold-compatible seed doc instead of a one-off markdown shape so\nthe first agent turn starts from the same document structure as every other\ninvestigation run.\n\nPer-session state and condensation reuse the existing pipeline unchanged:\n\n- `.git/entire-sessions/<session-id>.json` stores `Kind = \"agent_investigate\"`,\n  `InvestigatePrompt`, plus three new fields: `InvestigateRunID`,\n  `InvestigateRound`, `InvestigateTurn`, `InvestigateAgent`.\n- On the next user commit, the existing PostCommit condense path copies the\n  session into `entire/checkpoints/v1` with `Kind` and `ReviewSkills`-style\n  metadata fields propagated. Multi-session checkpoint format already supports\n  multiple sessions per checkpoint; each turn's session lands in its own\n  numbered subfolder (`0/`, `1/`, ...).\n\n### 4. Env-var handshake\n\nParallel package `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/env.go`:\n\n```go\nconst (\n    EnvSession      = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_SESSION\"      // \"1\"\n    EnvAgent        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_AGENT\"        // \"claude-code\"\n    EnvRunID        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_RUN_ID\"       // 12-hex\n    EnvRound        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_ROUND\"        // \"1\", \"2\", ...\n    EnvTurn         = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TURN\"         // overall turn index\n    EnvTopic        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TOPIC\"        // human-readable topic\n    EnvPrompt       = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_PROMPT\"       // composed prompt\n    EnvFindingsDoc  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_FINDINGS_DOC\" // absolute path\n    EnvTimelineDoc  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TIMELINE_DOC\" // absolute path\n    EnvStartingSHA  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_STARTING_SHA\" // anti-stale-env guard\n)\n```\n\n`AppendInvestigateEnv` mirrors `review.AppendReviewEnv`: strips any existing\n`ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` entries from `base`, then appends the contract\nvariables. Each spawned process inherits its own copy, so concurrent\nworktrees and concurrent investigations cannot leak env into each other.\n\n### 5. Loop architecture\n\nPort marvin's `runPlanLoop` into `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/loop.go`,\nspecialised to the investigate mode:\n\n```go\nfunc runInvestigateLoop(ctx context.Context, deps LoopDeps) (Result, error)\n```\n\nPer-turn flow:\n1. Hash findings doc + timeline before the turn and again after the turn, and\n   persist `PlanChanged` / `TimelineChanged`-style booleans in run state and\n   manifests for operator visibility. Mirror marvin's current bookkeeping here\n   instead of inventing extra control flow around \"no edit\" turns.\n2. Resolve the agent's spawner via `deps.SpawnerFor(agentName)` — this is\n   the new shared interface (see §6) that returns an `*exec.Cmd` builder.\n3. Compose the per-turn prompt via `ComposeInvestigatePrompt(in)` (port of\n   marvin's `buildInvestigatePrompt`, including the shared prior-decisions /\n   prior-claims / prior-fixes / memory-tools preamble plus the\n   investigate-specific body, with `Files: { Findings, Timeline }` pointing\n   at the worktree paths).\n4. Spawn the agent with `cmd.Stdout = MultiWriter(perTurnLogFile, optionalTeeStdout)`.\n5. After exit, parse the timeline file for the new `## Turn N — <agent>`\n   entry, read the `**Stance:**` line, and record it in run state. If the\n   header or stance line is missing/unparseable, record `unknown` and warn,\n   matching marvin's current parser behavior rather than synthesizing a fake\n   `request-changes` vote.\n6. Persist run state to `.git/entire-investigations/state/<run-id>.json` after\n   every turn so `--continue` can resume.\n\nLoop termination:\n- Quorum reached when the count of `approve` stances in the most recent\n  fully-played round is ≥ `quorum` (default `len(agents)`).\n- `paused` when ctx is cancelled (Ctrl+C) or an agent fails twice in a row.\n- `stalled` when `max-turns * len(agents)` turns have been played without\n  quorum.\n\nThe loop is single-threaded by design — each turn waits for the previous\nagent to exit before starting the next. This is the correct shape for\ninvestigate: agents must read each other's edits to make progress, so\nparallelism would hurt.\n\n### 6. Shared agent spawner\n\nRefactor opportunity: `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go` already\nencapsulates \"build *exec.Cmd from RunConfig\" via\n`ReviewerTemplate.BuildCmd`. Extract a smaller `Spawner` interface to\n`cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/` so both review and investigate consume it:\n\n```go\ntype Spawner interface {\n    Name() string\n    // BuildCmd returns a non-started exec.Cmd. The caller passes the\n    // composed env (already including ENTIRE_REVIEW_* or ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*\n    // produced by review.AppendReviewEnv / investigate.AppendInvestigateEnv)\n    // and the composed prompt. Spawner stays env-contract-agnostic.\n    BuildCmd(ctx context.Context, env []string, prompt string) *exec.Cmd\n}\n```\n\nPer-agent implementations live in each agent's package\n(`agent/claudecode/spawner.go`, `agent/codex/spawner.go`,\n`agent/geminicli/spawner.go`) and are tiny — the existing `buildReviewCmd`\nbodies (argv shape + stdin wiring) move here, with `AppendReviewEnv`\nfactored out to the caller. Review wraps a `Spawner` inside its existing\nparser-driven `ReviewerTemplate` (BuildCmd now reads `cfg.Prompt =\nComposeReviewPrompt(cfg)` then `env := AppendReviewEnv(os.Environ(),\nagentName, cfg, prompt); spawner.BuildCmd(ctx, env, prompt)`); investigate\nwraps the same `Spawner` with a log-file-piping driver and\n`AppendInvestigateEnv` instead. Review's existing argv contract tests\n(`agent/<name>/reviewer_test.go`) move to the spawner package and are\nre-pointed at the new helper, preserving the regression net.\n\nDo not reuse `agent.LauncherFor` for this path. The existing `LaunchCmd`\nimplementations in `agent/claudecode/claude.go`, `agent/codex/codex.go`, and\n`agent/geminicli/gemini.go` are foreground TTY-oriented entrypoints\n(`claude <prompt>`, `codex <prompt>`, `gemini <prompt>`) intended for normal\ninteractive coding sessions and `review --fix`, not for a headless loop that\nmust inject `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*`, capture deterministic stdout, and return\nwithout user keystrokes. Investigate needs the review-style non-interactive\nbuilders, not the interactive launcher contract.\n\nThis is a small refactor (≈ 60 LOC moved across three files) and is\nincluded in this PR because investigate cannot ship without a way to\nexec each agent non-interactively, and duplicating the argv constructors\nwould create the kind of drift the env-var contract is designed to prevent.\n\n### 7. Lifecycle adoption\n\nAdd `adoptInvestigateEnv(ctx, state, expectedAgent)` next to\n`adoptReviewEnv` in `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`. Same shape: short-circuit\nif state.Kind already set; check `EnvSession == \"1\"`; verify `EnvAgent` and\n`EnvStartingSHA` match; tag state.\n\n```go\nstate.Kind = session.KindAgentInvestigate\nstate.InvestigateRunID = os.Getenv(investigate.EnvRunID)\nstate.InvestigateRound = atoiOrZero(os.Getenv(investigate.EnvRound))\nstate.InvestigateTurn = atoiOrZero(os.Getenv(investigate.EnvTurn))\nstate.InvestigateTopic = os.Getenv(investigate.EnvTopic)\nstate.InvestigatePrompt = os.Getenv(investigate.EnvPrompt)\n```\n\nAdoption fires from the same `InitializeSession` site that calls\n`adoptReviewEnv` today, immediately after. `Kind` is single-valued, so a\nsession is either a review OR an investigate, never both.\n\n### 8. Checkpoint metadata changes\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`:\n- New const `KindAgentInvestigate Kind = \"agent_investigate\"`.\n- New method `Kind.IsInvestigate() bool { return k == KindAgentInvestigate }`.\n- New `State` fields: `InvestigateRunID`, `InvestigateRound`, `InvestigateTurn`,\n  `InvestigateTopic`, `InvestigatePrompt` (all `omitempty`).\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go`:\n- New `CommittedMetadata` fields parallel to `ReviewSkills` / `ReviewPrompt`:\n  `InvestigateRunID`, `InvestigateRound`, `InvestigateTurn`,\n  `InvestigateTopic`, `InvestigatePrompt`.\n- New `CheckpointSummary` field: `HasInvestigation bool` with `omitempty`.\n- Caller-side flag (matching `HasReview`): a new field\n  `WriteCommittedOptions.HasInvestigation` that the PostCommit dispatcher\n  computes via `state.Kind.IsInvestigate()` and propagates into the summary\n  the same way `HasReview` flows today.\n\n`committed.go`'s `WriteCommitted` propagates `HasInvestigation` with the\nexisting OR-style merge that protects `HasReview`: if a prior session in\nthis checkpoint already set the flag, keep it set.\n\nLocal readers must be updated explicitly; they do not \"just work\" today:\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/status.go` currently only consults `headHasReviewCheckpoint`.\n  Replace that single-purpose helper with a generic HEAD checkpoint summary\n  lookup (or parallel helpers backed by one lookup) so status can print\n  `Review` and `Investigation` lines independently when HEAD's checkpoint\n  summary carries either umbrella flag.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go` currently exposes `has_review` at the\n  top level and only review-specific session fields in its JSON envelope.\n  Add `has_investigation` plus session-level\n  `investigate_run_id`, `investigate_round`, `investigate_turn`, and\n  `investigate_topic` fields so `entire checkpoint explain --json` can show\n  the new metadata without requiring transcript reads.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go` can keep `InvestigatePrompt` out of the\n  JSON envelope, matching the current review export shape: prompt bodies are\n  available through transcript/prompt files when explicitly requested, but the\n  metadata export stays compact.\n\nBackwards compat: `omitempty` JSON tag means old metadata is read with\nzero values; old CLIs reading new metadata see `Kind = \"agent_investigate\"`\nas an unknown string and treat the session as \"normal\" — no review\nbehaviour fires, which is the correct fallback.\n\n`entire search` is intentionally not changed here. Its CLI surface talks to a\nremote search service with its own schema and ranking behavior; this PR only\nguarantees the local checkpoint metadata and manifests are present for future\nindexing, not that the cloud service grows an investigation-aware badge or\nfilter in lockstep.\n\n### 9. `--issue-link` semantics\n\nImplementation in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/issuelink.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc ResolveIssueLink(ctx context.Context, url string) (seedDoc []byte, topic string, err error)\n```\n\n1. Parse URL. If host is `github.com` and path matches\n   `/<owner>/<repo>/(issues|pull)/<n>`, dispatch to `gh issue view` or\n   `gh pr view` with `--json title,body,author,createdAt,labels,comments`.\n   Compose a markdown seed doc:\n\n   ```\n   # Investigation: <title>\n\n   **Source:** <url>\n   **Author:** @<author>\n   **Created:** <createdAt>\n   **Labels:** <labels>\n\n   ## Question\n\n   <body>\n\n   ## Comments\n\n   - **@<commenter> (<createdAt>):** <comment-body>\n   ...\n   ```\n\n2. If host is `github.com` but path doesn't match, return a clear error\n   pointing the user at `--topic` or seeding from a file.\n3. If host is anything else, return:\n   `\"--issue-link only supports GitHub issues and PRs in this release;\n    save the issue body to a file and pass it as a positional [seed-doc]\"`.\n4. If `gh` is not on PATH, return a clear error: `\"--issue-link requires\n    the gh CLI; install it (https://cli.github.com) or pass [seed-doc]\"`.\n\nThe `gh` invocation is wrapped in a `runGhFn` package var so unit tests can\ninject a fake. No HTTP client, no scraping, no auth handling — `gh` already\nowns auth and is the standard Entire users have.\n\nTopic derivation: prefer the issue/PR title; fall back to the URL itself if\nempty. The composed seed doc is written to `<findings-doc-path>` and the\nloop runs against it.\n\n### 10. `entire investigate fix` semantics\n\nMirrors `entire review --fix`. Resolves a manifest by `<run-id>` (or prompts\nto pick the most recent). Composes a follow-up prompt like:\n\n> A prior multi-agent investigation produced these findings. Use them as\n> grounded context to plan the next step. Do not re-investigate the same\n> question — assume the findings are correct unless you find direct\n> evidence to the contrary.\n>\n> ## Investigation findings\n>\n> <body of `.entire/investigations/<slug>.md`>\n>\n> ## Investigation timeline\n>\n> <body of `.entire/investigations/<slug>-timeline.md`>\n\nThen launches a normal `entire`-aware coding agent session via the existing\n`launchReviewFixAgent` helper, which is renamed `launchFixAgent` and moved\nfrom `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go` to a new `cmd/entire/cli/agentlaunch/`\npackage so both review-fix and investigate-fix can call it. The helper's\nenv-stripping step is broadened from `withoutReviewEnv` to also strip\n`ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` entries before exec, so a fix session never inherits\neither set of provenance env vars from its parent. The launched session is\na plain coding session, not tagged as review or investigate.\n\nThis is \"the way to feed a saved investigation back into a follow-up agent\nrun for context\" called for in the goals.\n\n### 11. Picker / first-run setup\n\n`runInvestigateConfigPicker` in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/picker.go`:\n\n- Lists agents that are both launchable and hook-installed in the current\n  repo (filters via `SpawnerFor != nil` plus the same hook-installed check\n  review uses).\n- Multi-select — needs at least one selection.\n- Asks for max-turns (default 3) and quorum (default 0 = all).\n- Saves to `EntireSettings.Investigate`.\n\n`ConfirmFirstRunSetup` mirrors review's: when `entire investigate` runs with\nno config, print a banner explaining that we're configuring before running,\nget y/N confirmation, run the picker, then drop into the loop.\n\n### 12. Backwards compat / migrations\n\n- New JSON fields all carry `omitempty`; old metadata reads with zero values.\n- `Kind` is a string; the new `\"agent_investigate\"` value is ignored by old\n  CLIs, which treat the session as untagged (normal).\n- No file format migrations. No state-file rewrites. No\n  `entire/checkpoints/v1` rewrites.\n- The shared-spawner refactor (§6) preserves identical argv for review;\n  contract tests pin the exact argv per agent so we'd catch any drift in CI.\n\n### 13. Telemetry / logging\n\n- All logging uses the existing `logging` package with structured slog\n  attrs (`event`, `agent`, `round`, `turn`, `run_id`, `outcome`).\n- No external telemetry transports added. The existing\n  `__send_analytics` path picks up the new event names via its lowercase\n  command-name prefix without any code change in the analytics sender.\n- Privacy: per CLAUDE.md, we never log prompts, file bodies, or commit\n  messages — only operational metadata (counts, IDs, paths, durations).\n\n### 14. Testing strategy\n\nAll in this PR.\n\n**Unit tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/`:\n- `prompt_test.go`: golden-file tests for `ComposeInvestigatePrompt` covering\n  first round, mid-loop turn, with/without `always_prompt`, with prior\n  reviewer comments, and with prior decisions / claims / fixes so the shared\n  prompt preamble is pinned alongside the investigate body.\n- `bootstrap_test.go`: seed-doc passthrough, scaffold rendering with\n  `## Prior Entire Context`, and topic derivation from `# Investigation:`,\n  first H1, then filename fallback.\n- `env_test.go`: `EncodeXxx` / `DecodeXxx` round-trips, `AppendInvestigateEnv`\n  strips stale entries, `isInvestigateEnvEntry` true/false table.\n- `issuelink_test.go`: URL parsing table (issue vs PR vs unsupported host\n  vs malformed), fake-`gh` injection produces expected seed-doc body, error\n  paths surface actionable messages.\n- `loop_test.go`: `runInvestigateLoop` with a fake spawner that produces\n  scripted timeline edits per turn — verifies quorum detection, max-turns\n  termination, paused-on-second-failure, `unknown` stance fallback,\n  changed-file booleans, and resume from state file.\n- `parse_stance_test.go`: scans timeline for `**Stance:**` lines, tolerant\n  of whitespace and mixed dash separators in headings.\n\n**Lifecycle tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`:\n- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_Success` — env vars set, state tagged.\n- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_AgentMismatch` — env from a different agent does\n  not tag the session.\n- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_StaleStartingSHA` — base-commit guard.\n- `TestAdoptInvestigateEnv_AlreadyTaggedNotOverwritten` — review session is\n  not silently re-kinded.\n\n**Checkpoint tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`:\n- `TestCommittedMetadata_AgentInvestigate` — JSON wire-format pin.\n- `TestCheckpointSummary_HasInvestigation` — JSON wire-format pin including\n  `omitempty` zero-value behaviour, mirroring `TestCheckpointSummary_HasReview`.\n\n**Spawner refactor regression tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/`:\n- `TestClaudeCodeSpawner_ArgvUnchanged`,\n  `TestCodexSpawner_ArgvUnchanged`,\n  `TestGeminiCLISpawner_ArgvUnchanged` — golden-file pins of the exact argv\n  produced for each agent given a fixed prompt and env, so review's pre-refactor\n  argv stays byte-identical post-refactor. These pins replace the existing\n  `agent/<name>/reviewer_test.go` argv assertions.\n\n**Reader / UX tests**:\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export_test.go`: pins the new\n  `has_investigation`, `investigate_run_id`, `investigate_round`,\n  `investigate_turn`, and `investigate_topic` JSON fields and their\n  `omitempty` behavior.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/status_test.go` (or the generalized HEAD-checkpoint helper\n  tests if that logic moves out of `status.go`): verifies status prints the\n  new `Investigation · investigated (checkpoint <id>)` line, and that review +\n  investigation can coexist in the rendered status output without one hiding\n  the other.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/attach_test.go`: extends the existing review-attach surface\n  coverage with investigate tagging through the generalized attach path.\n\n**Integration tests** in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`:\n- `TestInvestigate_EnvVarAdoptionCondensesMetadataOnNextCommit` — modeled on\n  `integration_test/review_test.go`: set `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` on a simulated\n  hook event, assert the session state is tagged as investigate, then commit\n  and verify `HasInvestigation` plus the investigate metadata fields on the\n  checkpoint.\n- `TestInvestigateCommand_PassesInvestigateEnvToSpawnedAgentHooks` — also\n  modeled on the review integration path, but with fake `claude` / `codex`\n  binaries on `PATH`. Each fake binary appends one turn entry to the\n  findings/timeline files, calls `\"$ENTIRE_TEST_BINARY\" hooks <agent>\n  user-prompt-submit`, then exits 0. This verifies the real cobra command,\n  spawner wiring, and env-var handshake without any API calls.\n- `TestInvestigateAttach_TagsAttachedSessionAsInvestigate` — attaches a saved\n  transcript post-hoc and asserts the checkpoint/session metadata records\n  `Kind = agent_investigate`.\n- `TestInvestigate_Continue_Resumes` — seed a run-state file plus findings and\n  timeline docs, then resume with fake spawned agents and verify the next\n  expected turn is played instead of replaying completed turns.\n- `TestInvestigate_IssueLink_GhFake` — fake `gh` binary on PATH returns a\n  fixture issue body; verify seed doc bootstrap.\n\n**No new E2E canary in this PR.** Vogon is intentionally test-only,\nnon-launchable, and `AreHooksInstalled()` returns false, so it cannot satisfy\nthe same preflight path the real command will use. Real-agent E2E remains\nopt-in per repo policy; the product verification bar here is unit tests plus\nthe fake-binary integration harness above.\n\n### 15. Files added / modified\n\nNew files (all under `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/`):\n- `cmd.go` — cobra wiring, `NewCommand(deps)`, flag parsing.\n- `loop.go` — `runInvestigateLoop`, per-turn driver, stance parsing.\n- `prompt.go` — `ComposeInvestigatePrompt`.\n- `env.go` — env var constants + helpers.\n- `picker.go` — first-run config picker.\n- `manifest.go` — local manifest read/write (mirrors review).\n- `fix.go` — `entire investigate fix` subcommand.\n- `attach.go` — `entire investigate attach <session-id>`.\n- `findings.go` — `--findings` browser.\n- `issuelink.go` — GitHub issue/PR resolver via `gh`.\n- `state.go` — `RunState` JSON read/write.\n- Plus matching `_test.go` files per §14.\n\nNew files under `cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/`:\n- `spawn.go` — `Spawner` interface, registry helper.\n- `spawner_test.go` — `Test<Agent>Spawner_ArgvUnchanged` golden-file pins.\n- Per-agent: small additions to `agent/claudecode/spawner.go`,\n  `agent/codex/spawner.go`, `agent/geminicli/spawner.go` (move existing\n  `buildReviewCmd` argv construction here and parameterise by env).\n\nNew file `cmd/entire/cli/agentlaunch/launch.go`:\n- `launchFixAgent(ctx, agentName, prompt) error` — moved from\n  `review/fix.go:launchReviewFixAgent`, with env stripping broadened to\n  cover both `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` and `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*`.\n\nModified existing files:\n- `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go` — append `investigate` to `experimentalCommands`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` and a new `investigate_bridge.go` glue file —\n  wire `investigate.NewCommand(...)` plus the CLI-package deps it needs.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go` — call `adoptInvestigateEnv` next to\n  `adoptReviewEnv`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go` — add `KindAgentInvestigate`,\n  `Kind.IsInvestigate()`, new state fields.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go` — add `HasInvestigation`,\n  investigate metadata fields.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` — propagate `HasInvestigation`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go` — surface investigate fields in JSON\n  export.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` — add `Investigate` field +\n  helper accessors.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/status.go` and the helper that reads HEAD checkpoint\n  summary flags — surface investigation state next to review state.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/attach.go` — generalize the attach path so investigate\n  attach can tag a session and write investigate metadata.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go` and the per-agent\n  `reviewer.go` files — wrap the new `Spawner` instead of inlining argv.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go` — call into\n  `agentlaunch.launchFixAgent` instead of the local\n  `launchReviewFixAgent`; remove the now-shared body.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/investigate_test.go` — fake-binary\n  command/integration coverage for the new loop.\n- `CLAUDE.md` — append an `entire investigate` section parallel to\n  `entire review`.\n\nApproximate diff size: ~1,700 lines added (≈ 1,100 product, ≈ 600 tests),\n~200 lines moved/refactored for the spawner extraction, the\n`launchReviewFixAgent` → `agentlaunch.launchFixAgent` move, and the\nHEAD-checkpoint helper generalization. One PR.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n**1. Run agents in parallel (not round-robin).** Rejected. Agents must read\neach other's findings to converge; parallel runs would either produce\nnon-overlapping findings (no convergence) or require a merge step that\nre-introduces sequential editing. Marvin chose round-robin for the same\nreason.\n\n**2. Store findings in `~/.entire/investigations/` like marvin does in\n`~/.marvin/`.** Rejected. Entire is per-repo and ties context to\ncheckpoints; a per-repo path under `.entire/` (worktree) and\n`.git/entire-investigations/` (state) keeps everything addressable from the\nrepo and survives the same way checkpoints do. Marvin's global home was\nappropriate for a multi-repo POC; entire's model is repo-scoped.\n\n**3. Reuse `Kind = \"agent_review\"` and extend `IsReview()` to cover\ninvestigate, with a new sub-discriminator.** Rejected. Review and\ninvestigate produce different artifacts (skills output vs findings doc),\nhave different commit-time UX (re-run guard wording, status banner), and\nthe existing `HasReview` docstring explicitly says it's the umbrella for\n\"any review happened\". Conflating the two breaks the umbrella's meaning\nand forces every downstream reader to disambiguate. A parallel\n`HasInvestigation` flag is simpler.\n\n**4. Build a generic web fetcher behind `--issue-link`.** Rejected per\nnon-goals. `gh` already handles GitHub auth, rate limits, and JSON output;\nnon-GitHub hosts (Linear, GitLab, Jira) need different auth models and\nresponse shapes that do not generalise. A pluggable fetcher framework is\nreal engineering and not something we can afford to ship correctly inside\nthis PR. Users with non-GitHub sources can pre-paste content into a seed\nfile in two seconds.\n\n**5. Live overview TUI like marvin's `investigate_tui.go`.** Rejected per\nthe user's explicit \"don't do tui\". The non-TUI design also unblocks\nrunning investigate inside another agent session (e.g. a Claude Code\nsession calling `entire investigate` via Bash) — TUI sinks block on\nkeypresses that never arrive in that context. Per-turn log files are\ngreppable, archivable, and visible without ANSI gymnastics.\n\n**6. Skip the spawner refactor; duplicate argv builders for investigate.**\nRejected. Three agents × two callers (review + investigate) = six places\nwhere argv must stay aligned. The next agent-flag tweak (e.g. a future\n`--permission-mode` change) would silently drift across callers. Sharing\nthrough a small `Spawner` interface costs ≈ 60 LOC and prevents the drift.\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n- **Risk: `gh` not installed.** Detected at `--issue-link` resolution time;\n  surface a clear error pointing at the `gh` install URL and the seed-doc\n  fallback. Not blocking for the rest of the command.\n- **Risk: agent fails to modify the findings doc.** The pre-turn hash check\n  still detects \"no edit\", but the loop should surface that as bookkeeping\n  (`PlanChanged=false` / `TimelineChanged=false`) plus an `unknown` stance\n  warning when the timeline entry is missing, rather than inventing a vote the\n  agent never cast. This keeps the control flow aligned with marvin's current\n  behavior while still making silent turns obvious in logs and manifests.\n- **Risk: stale `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` env from a parent shell tagging the\n  wrong session.** Same protection as review: `EnvAgent` must match the\n  hook's agent and `EnvStartingSHA` must match the session's base commit.\n  Both must hold for adoption to fire; either mismatch leaves the session\n  untagged with a logged warning.\n- **Risk: the shared spawner refactor regresses review argv.** Contract\n  tests in `agent/<name>/spawner_test.go` pin the exact argv string per\n  agent; review's existing argv tests (e.g. `claudecode/reviewer_test.go`)\n  also serve as a regression net via the wrapper.\n- **Risk: investigation findings doc lands in the user's commit\n  unintentionally.** Entire does not guarantee `.entire/` is ignored in every\n  repo, and this repo's tracked `.gitignore` does not ignore it today. The\n  findings doc is still a deliberate deliverable, so we do not auto-add a\n  gitignore entry or auto-stage it; we surface the file path on completion so\n  users can choose whether to commit it or ignore `.entire/investigations/`\n  explicitly in their own repo.\n- **Risk: `entire investigate` invoked from inside an existing agent\n  session (Claude Code calling Bash → entire investigate).** Works by\n  design — no TUI, env per process — but the inner sessions inherit\n  `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` if the outer was a review. The\n  `withoutReviewEnv`-style strip in `AppendInvestigateEnv` removes any\n  `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` entries before appending investigate vars to prevent\n  cross-tagging.\n- **Risk: product plan overpromises cloud search behavior that this repo\n  cannot ship.** Mitigation: scope the PR to local checkpoint/manifests UX\n  only (`status`, `checkpoint explain`, `--findings`, `fix`) and document\n  that dedicated `entire search` investigation surfacing depends on the\n  remote service, so it is not part of this change set.\n\n## Decision\n\nApproved direction: ship as a single PR titled `feat(investigate): add\nentire investigate command (labs)`. Includes the cobra command, the loop\ndriver, the env-var contract, the lifecycle adoption, the\n`HasInvestigation` summary flag, the status / explain-export surfacing, the\nshared spawner refactor, the `--issue-link` resolver, the `fix` and\n`attach` subcommands, the picker, the manifest reader, the fake-binary\nintegration coverage, and the CLAUDE.md update.\n\nReviewer focus areas:\n- Env-var contract correctness (multi-tenant inheritance, stale-env\n  protection).\n- Lifecycle adoption ordering vs `adoptReviewEnv`.\n- Checkpoint metadata back-compat (old CLI reading new metadata).\n- Spawner refactor preserves exact argv per agent.\n- `--issue-link` URL parsing rejects malformed inputs.\n","numLines":767,"startLine":1,"totalLines":767}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"efa77e89-e428-4ff6-9b0f-348ef3180b3b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/entire-labs-investigate","sessionId":"3fbfb7fc-97be-4ee0-8910-deccdd0efe9c","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"entire-labs-investigate"}
