teTopic string` (`json:\"investigate_topic,omitempty\"`)\n  - `InvestigatePrompt string` (`json:\"investigate_prompt,omitempty\"`)\n\nEach field needs a doc comment in the same style as `ReviewSkills`/`ReviewPrompt`. Keep `Kind` single-valued (a session is review OR investigate, not both).\n\n### 2. `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go` — add HasInvestigation + investigate metadata fields\n\nThree changes, all parallel to the existing review fields:\n\n(a) `WriteCommittedOptions` struct currently has fields `Kind string`, `ReviewSkills []string`, `ReviewPrompt string`, `HasReview bool`. Add (next to those):\n```go\nInvestigateRunID  string\nInvestigateRound  int\nInvestigateTurn   int\nInvestigateTopic  string\nInvestigatePrompt string\nHasInvestigation  bool\n```\n\n(b) `CommittedMetadata` struct currently has `Kind`, `ReviewSkills`, `ReviewPrompt` (with `omitempty` JSON tags). Add (next to those):\n```go\nInvestigateRunID  string `json:\"investigate_run_id,omitempty\"`\nInvestigateRound  int    `json:\"investigate_round,omitempty\"`\nInvestigateTurn   int    `json:\"investigate_turn,omitempty\"`\nInvestigateTopic  string `json:\"investigate_topic,omitempty\"`\nInvestigatePrompt string `json:\"investigate_prompt,omitempty\"`\n```\n\n(c) `CheckpointSummary` struct has `HasReview bool \\`json:\"has_review,omitempty\"\\``. Add immediately after it:\n```go\nHasInvestigation bool `json:\"has_investigation,omitempty\"`\n```\n\nEach new field needs a doc comment that mirrors the equivalent Review/`HasReview` doc.\n\n### 3. `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` — add Investigate config\n\nCurrently the file has `Review map[string]ReviewConfig` and a `ReviewConfig` struct with `Skills []string` and `Prompt string`. The plan says investigate is **different by design** — investigate runs the same shared prompt across all agents, so per-agent customization isn't needed. The schema is a flat list:\n\nAdd near `Review`:\n```go\n// Investigate holds configuration for `entire investigate`. Empty means\n// `entire investigate` triggers the first-run picker.\nInvestigate *InvestigateConfig `json:\"investigate,omitempty\"`\n```\n\nAdd a new struct:\n```go\n// InvestigateConfig holds the configuration for `entire investigate`.\n// Unlike ReviewConfig, investigate runs the same shared prompt across\n// all configured agents, so the schema is a flat agent list with global\n// loop knobs rather than per-agent skill lists.\ntype InvestigateConfig struct {\n    // Agents is the ordered list of agent names to round-robin during the loop.\n    Agents []string `json:\"agents,omitempty\"`\n\n    // MaxTurns is the per-agent turn budget. Defaults to 3 when zero.\n    MaxTurns int `json:\"max_turns,omitempty\"`\n\n    // Quorum is the count of `approve` stances needed to terminate the loop.\n    // Zero means \"all agents must approve\" (matches marvin's default).\n    Quorum int `json:\"quorum,omitempty\"`\n\n    // AlwaysPrompt is appended to every turn's composed prompt, parallel\n    // to ReviewConfig.Prompt.\n    AlwaysPrompt string `json:\"always_prompt,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// IsZero reports whether the config is effectively unset.\nfunc (c *InvestigateConfig) IsZero() bool {\n    if c == nil {\n        return true\n    }\n    return len(c.Agents) == 0 && c.MaxTurns == 0 && c.Quorum == 0 && c.AlwaysPrompt == \"\"\n}\n```\n\nAdd a helper `func (s *EntireSettings) InvestigateConfig() *InvestigateConfig` that returns `s.Investigate` (handling nil receiver), parallel to `ReviewConfigFor`.\n\nThe settings package uses a `mergeJSON` helper; check whether `Investigate` needs explicit handling there. If `mergeJSON` parses unknown keys via the temp `EntireSettings` and discards anything not explicitly merged, you may need to add an `Investigate` merge step. Read `mergeJSON` and the helpers it calls (`mergeScalarFields`, `mergeStrategyOptions`, `mergeSummaryGeneration`, `mergeRedaction`, `mergeCommitLinking`) to confirm. If `Investigate` is not picked up automatically, add a merge step that takes the override's value as-is (whole-object replacement) when present.\n\n### 4. `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/env.go` — env-var contract (NEW PACKAGE)\n\nThis is a brand-new package. Mirror `cmd/entire/cli/review/env.go` very closely. Defining:\n\n```go\npackage investigate\n\nconst (\n    EnvSession      = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_SESSION\"      // \"1\"\n    EnvAgent        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_AGENT\"        // \"claude-code\"\n    EnvRunID        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_RUN_ID\"       // 12-hex\n    EnvRound        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_ROUND\"        // \"1\", \"2\", ...\n    EnvTurn         = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TURN\"         // overall turn index\n    EnvTopic        = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TOPIC\"        // human-readable topic\n    EnvPrompt       = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_PROMPT\"       // composed prompt\n    EnvFindingsDoc  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_FINDINGS_DOC\" // absolute path\n    EnvTimelineDoc  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TIMELINE_DOC\" // absolute path\n    EnvStartingSHA  = \"ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_STARTING_SHA\" // anti-stale-env guard\n)\n```\n\nAdd helpers parallel to review's:\n\n```go\n// AppendInvestigateEnv adds the ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_* env vars to base, returning\n// the new slice. Strips any pre-existing ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_* AND ENTIRE_REVIEW_*\n// entries before appending. Stripping ENTIRE_REVIEW_* prevents an outer review\n// session from mis-tagging a child investigate session if invoked nested.\ntype AppendOptions struct {\n    AgentName    string\n    RunID        string\n    Round        int\n    Turn         int\n    Topic        string\n    Prompt       string\n    FindingsDoc  string\n    TimelineDoc  string\n    StartingSHA  string\n}\nfunc AppendInvestigateEnv(base []string, opts AppendOptions) []string\n\n// IsInvestigateEnvEntry reports whether kv is an ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_* entry.\nfunc IsInvestigateEnvEntry(kv string) bool\n```\n\n**Important:** the strip step must remove BOTH `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` an