ute path to timeline doc\n}\n\n// ComposeInvestigatePrompt builds the prompt sent to an agent for one turn.\n// The agent reads the findings + timeline files, edits them in place, and\n// records its stance in the timeline.\nfunc ComposeInvestigatePrompt(in ComposeInput) string\n```\n\nThe prompt body should:\n1. Tell the agent it is participating in a multi-agent investigation, what its role is (skeptical investigator).\n2. Reference the Files.Findings and Files.Timeline absolute paths and instruct the agent to read both before editing.\n3. Explain the **Stance** convention: the agent must record one of `approve` / `request-changes` / `abstain` in a `**Stance:**` line under a new `## Turn N — <agent>` heading in the timeline doc.\n4. Include round/turn metadata so the agent knows which turn it is.\n5. Append `AlwaysPrompt` verbatim if non-empty.\n6. Include `PriorContext` verbatim if non-empty (formatted as a `## Prior context` block).\n\nMarvin's prompt has a \"shared preamble\" that includes prior decisions, prior claims, prior fixes, and memory tools. **Skip the marvin memory pieces** — entire doesn't have those. Keep the investigate-specific body and add a placeholder for `PriorContext` instead.\n\nAdd comprehensive golden-file tests in `prompt_test.go`:\n- `TestComposeInvestigatePrompt_FirstRound` — Round 1, Turn 1, no AlwaysPrompt, no PriorContext.\n- `TestComposeInvestigatePrompt_MidLoop` — Round 2, Turn 5.\n- `TestComposeInvestigatePrompt_WithAlwaysPrompt` — AlwaysPrompt set.\n- `TestComposeInvestigatePrompt_WithPriorContext` — PriorContext set.\n\nUse `testutil.AssertGolden` if available (search `cmd/entire/cli/testutil/` for golden helpers); otherwise check golden via direct string comparison. Save golden files at `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/testdata/prompt-*.txt`. (Use `update := flag.Bool(\"update\", false, \"update golden files\")` pattern if you want, but inline string comparison is fine.)\n\n### 2. `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/bootstrap.go`\n\nBootstrap implements: \"given the user's `[seed-doc]` / `--topic` / `--issue-link` input, produce the initial findings doc + timeline doc on disk.\"\n\n```go\n// BootstrapInput configures the initial findings doc + timeline doc.\ntype BootstrapInput struct {\n    // Exactly one of SeedDoc / Topic / IssueLinkSeed must be set.\n    SeedDoc       string  // absolute path to a user-provided seed doc, or empty\n    Topic         string  // user-provided --topic, or empty\n    IssueLinkSeed []byte  // markdown produced by ResolveIssueLink (issuelink.go)\n    IssueLinkTopic string // topic derived from --issue-link (issue/PR title)\n\n    // Output destinations (absolute paths).\n    FindingsDoc string\n    TimelineDoc string\n\n    // Prior-context block to inject when scaffolding (may be empty).\n    PriorEntireContext string\n}\n\n// BootstrapResult reports what was produced.\ntype BootstrapResult struct {\n    Topic       string  // resolved topic (used for slug/manifest)\n    FindingsDoc string  // absolute path written\n    TimelineDoc string  // absolute path written\n}\n\n// Bootstrap writes the initial findings doc and timeline doc to disk.\n//   - SeedDoc: copy verbatim into FindingsDoc, derive topic from\n//     \"# Investigation: ...\" heading, then first H1, then filename.\n//   - IssueLinkSeed: write the bytes to FindingsDoc; topic = IssueLinkTopic.\n//   - Topic only (no seed): render a scaffold with sections TLDR, Question,\n//     Prior work, System under investigation, Approach, Findings,\n//     Unknowns / Assumptions, Conclusion. If PriorEntireContext is non-empty,\n//     insert it as a \"## Prior Entire Context\" block after Question.\n// Always writes an empty TimelineDoc with just the heading.\nfunc Bootstrap(ctx context.Context, in BootstrapInput) (BootstrapResult, error)\n\n// SlugifyTopic converts a topic string into a filesystem-safe slug\n// (lowercase, alphanumeric + dashes). Mirrors marvin's slugifyTopic.\nfunc SlugifyTopic(topic string) string\n\n// DeriveTopicFromSeed extracts a topic from a seed doc body. Order:\n//   1. \"# Investigation: <topic>\" line\n//   2. First \"# <topic>\" heading\n//   3. Filename (without extension)\nfunc DeriveTopicFromSeed(body []byte, fallbackFilename string) string\n```\n\nTests in `bootstrap_test.go`:\n- `TestBootstrap_SeedDocPassthrough` — verbatim copy, topic from \"# Investigation:\" heading.\n- `TestBootstrap_TopicScaffold` — scaffold sections present, no PriorEntireContext block.\n- `TestBootstrap_TopicScaffoldWithPriorEntireContext` — PriorEntireContext rendered.\n- `TestBootstrap_IssueLinkSeed` — issue-link bytes written verbatim, topic from IssueLinkTopic.\n- `TestDeriveTopicFromSeed` — table test for \"# Investigation:\" / first \"# H1\" / filename fallback.\n- `TestSlugifyTopic` — table test for spaces/punct/unicode/empty.\n\n### 3. `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/manifest.go`\n\nMirror `cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go` very closely. Read that file first.\n\nThe local manifest is a JSON record persisted at `<git-common-dir>/entire-investigations/manifests/<timestamp>-<run-id>.json` for `--findings` browsing.\n\n```go\n// LocalManifest is the persisted record of one investigate run for local\n// findings browsing (entire investigate --findings).\ntype LocalManifest struct {\n    RunID        string    `json:\"run_id\"`\n    Topic        string    `json:\"topic\"`\n    Slug         string    `json:\"slug\"`\n    StartingSHA  string    `json:\"starting_sha\"`\n    WorktreePath string    `json:\"worktree_path,omitempty\"`\n    FindingsDoc  string    `json:\"findings_doc,omitempty\"`  // absolute or repo-relative\n    TimelineDoc  string    `json:\"timeline_doc,omitempty\"`\n    Agents       []string  `json:\"agents\"`\n    Outcome      string    `json:\"outcome\"`                  // \"quorum\", \"stalled\", \"paused\", \"cancelled\"\n    StancesByAgent map[string]string `json:\"stances_by_agent,omitempty\"` // last stance per agent\n    StartedAt    time.Time `json:\"started_at\"`\n    EndedAt      time.Time `json:\"ended_at\"`\n}\n\n// LocalManifestStore wraps the manifests directory.\ntype LocalManifestStore struct{ dir string }\n\nfunc NewLocalManifestStore(ctx context.Context) (*LocalManifestStore, error)\nfunc NewLocalManifestStoreWithDir(dir string) *LocalManifestStore\n\nfunc (s *LocalManifestStore) Write(ctx context.Context, m LocalManifest) error\nfunc (s *LocalManifestStore) List(ctx context.Context) ([]LocalManifest, error) // sorted newest first\nfunc (s *LocalManifestStore) FindByRunID(ctx context.Context, runID string) (LocalManifest, bool, error)\n```\n\nTests in `manifest_test.go`:\n- `TestLocalManifestStore_RoundTrip` — Write then List returns the manifest.\n- `TestLocalManifestStore_ListSortedNewestFirst` — multiple writes, sort order pinned.\n- `TestLocalManifestStore_FindByRunID` — found vs not-found vs sentinel-empty cases.\n- `TestLocalManifestStore_MissingDirReturnsEmpty` — NewLocalManifestStoreWithDir to a nonexistent dir + List = empty slice, no error.\n\n### 4. `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/issuelink.go`\n\nResolve a GitHub issue or PR URL into a seed-doc body suitable for Bootstrap.\n\n```go\n// IssueLinkResult is the output of ResolveIssueLink.\ntype IssueLinkResult struct {\n    SeedDoc []byte // markdown bytes ready to write to the findings doc\n    Topic   string // human-readable topic (issue/PR title, fallback to URL)\n}\n\n// ResolveIssueLink resolves a GitHub issue or PR URL via the gh CLI.\n// On non-GitHub hosts or malformed paths, returns an actionable error\n// pointing the user at --topic or [seed-doc].\nfunc ResolveIssueLink(ctx context.Context, url string) (IssueLinkResult, error)\n\n// runGhFn is the package-level hook tests inject. Production wires this to a\n// real `gh` exec. See gh helper below.\nvar runGhFn = runGhExec\n\n// ghIssue / ghPR are the JSON shapes ResolveIssueLink unmarshals into.\ntype ghIssue struct {\n    Title     string    `json:\"title\"`\n    Body      string    `json:\"body\"`\n    Author    ghUser    `json:\"author\"`\n    CreatedAt time.Time `json:\"createdAt\"`\n    Labels    []ghLabel `json:\"labels\"`\n    Comments  []ghComment `json:\"comments\"`\n}\n// (similar for PRs; you can reuse ghIssue if the JSON shapes are compatible)\n\ntype ghUser struct{ Login string `json:\"login\"` }\ntype ghLabel struct{ Name string `json:\"name\"` }\ntype ghComment struct {\n    Author    ghUser    `json:\"author\"`\n    CreatedAt time.Time `json:\"createdAt\"`\n    Body      string    `json:\"body\"`\n}\n```\n\nBehavior:\n1. Parse URL with `net/url`. Reject if Host != \"github.com\".\n2. Match path against `/<owner>/<repo>/(issues|pull|pulls)/<n>$` (allow `pull` and `pulls`).\n3. Dispatch:\n   - `issues` → `gh issue view <url> --json title,body,author,createdAt,labels,comments`\n   - `pull`/`pulls` → `gh pr view <url> --json title,body,author,createdAt,labels,comments`\n4. Compose seed doc:\n   ```\n   # Investigation: <title>\n\n   **Source:** <url>\n   **Author:** @<login>\n   **Created:** <iso-date>\n   **Labels:** <comma-joined>\n\n   ## Question\n\n   <body>\n\n   ## Comments\n\n   - **@<login> (<iso-date>):** <comment-body>\n   ...\n   ```\n5. Topic: prefer title; fall back to URL.\n6. Errors:\n   - `gh` not on PATH (`exec.LookPath`): return `\"--issue-link requires the gh CLI; install it (https://cli.github.com) or pass [seed-doc]\"`.\n   - Non-GitHub host: `\"--issue-link only supports GitHub issues and PRs in this release; save the issue body to a file and pass it as a positional [seed-doc]\"`.\n   - GitHub but malformed path: `\"--issue-link expects a GitHub issue or PR URL; got <path>\"`.\n\nHelper:\n\n```go\n// runGhExec is the production runGhFn. Returns gh's stdout bytes, or an\n// error wrapping exec.ExitError with stderr captured.\nfunc runGhExec(ctx context.Context, args ...string) ([]byte, error)\n```\n\nTests in `issuelink_test.go`:\n- `TestResolveIssueLink_Issue` — fake runGhFn returns a fixture issue JSON; assert seed-doc body and topic.\n- `TestResolveIssueLink_PR` — same for PR.\n- `TestResolveIssueLink_RejectsNonGitHub` — gitlab.com URL returns the actionable error.\n- `TestResolveIssueLink_RejectsMalformedPath` — github.com URL with /tree/main returns the actionable error.\n- `TestResolveIssueLink_GhMissing` — set runGhFn to a stub that returns ErrGhNotFound (you can define a sentinel for this), assert the error message points at the install URL.\n- (Skip a real-`gh` integration test; production gh is exercised by the integration test in Task 11.)\n\nFor tests, inject the fake via `t.Cleanup(func() { runGhFn = runGhExec })` after overriding it.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Read CLAUDE.md at the repo root before starting. Follow project conventions (`t.Parallel()`, `testutil` helpers, no committing CLAUDE.md changes).\n- Do NOT import the review package — investigate stays standalone (see Task 1's env.go for how it strips review env without importing).\n- Tests must call `t.Parallel()`.\n- Don't commit. Leave changes uncommitted.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test -- ./cmd/entire/cli/investigate/...\n```\n\nIf lint changes pass after fmt, re-run lint on the formatted tree before declaring done.\n\n## Reporting\n\nReport DONE / DONE_WITH_CONCERNS / BLOCKED / NEEDS_CONTEXT. List files created, tests added, and verification output.","agentId":"a54a38757056d488a","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All pass. \n\n## DONE\n\n### Files created (in `/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/entire-labs-investigate/cmd/entire/cli/investigate/`)\n\n**Source files**\n- `prompt.go` — `ComposeInvestigatePrompt`, `ComposeInput`, `Files` for per-turn prompt rendering. Skips marvin's memory blocks; supports `AlwaysPrompt` and an optional `PriorContext` block.\n- `bootstrap.go` — `Bootstrap`, `BootstrapInput`, `BootstrapResult`, `SlugifyTopic`, `DeriveTopicFromSeed`. Three-mode bootstrap: seed-doc verbatim, issue-link bytes verbatim