{"parentUuid":"4dfa2b6a-0ae3-4974-b670-ea767ff910b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019Jn4NC8RRmPmMnD4q2Gcgi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014zS91o1KPYGexsJQuSM4PD","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement Task 4: investigate loop driver","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are implementing Task 4 of a larger plan: the round-robin investigation loop driver in `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/loop.go`.\n\nWorking directory: /Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/entire-labs-investigate\n\n## Context\n\nWe're shipping `entire investigate` — a sibling of `entire review` that runs a multi-agent investigation. Earlier tasks set up the data model and primitives:\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/env.go` — env-var contract: `EnvSession`, `EnvAgent`, `EnvRunID`, `EnvRound`, `EnvTurn`, `EnvTopic`, `EnvPrompt`, `EnvFindingsDoc`, `EnvTimelineDoc`, `EnvStartingSHA`, plus `AppendInvestigateEnv(base []string, opts AppendOptions) []string`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/state.go` — `RunState`, `TurnStance`, `StateStore` for persistence at `<git-common-dir>/entire-investigations/state/<run-id>.json`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/prompt.go` — `ComposeInvestigatePrompt(in ComposeInput) string` with fields Topic/AgentName/Round/Turn/AlwaysPrompt/Files/PriorContext.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/spawn/spawn.go` — `Spawner` interface with `BuildCmd(ctx, env, prompt) *exec.Cmd`. Per-agent implementations in `agent/claudecode/spawner.go`, `agent/codex/spawner.go`, `agent/geminicli/spawner.go`.\n\nRead these five files first to confirm the exact APIs.\n\n## What to build\n\nA round-robin loop that, for each turn:\n1. Hashes findings + timeline files (SHA-256) before the turn.\n2. Composes the prompt via `ComposeInvestigatePrompt`.\n3. Builds env via `AppendInvestigateEnv(os.Environ(), AppendOptions{...})`.\n4. Spawns the agent via `Spawner.BuildCmd`.\n5. Pipes the agent's stdout to a per-turn log file (and optionally tees to a Writer for `--verbose`).\n6. Waits for the agent to exit. Re-hashes the docs.\n7. Parses the timeline doc for the new `## Turn N — <agent>` block; reads the `**Stance:**` line. Falls back to `unknown` if missing.\n8. Appends a `TurnStance` to `RunState.Stances`, persists state.\n9. Decides terminate / continue.\n\nThe loop is **single-threaded**. Each turn waits for the previous to exit before starting.\n\n## Public API\n\n```go\npackage investigate\n\n// LoopDeps collects the runtime-injectable hooks runInvestigateLoop needs.\n// Tests inject fakes for SpawnerFor, RunGitFn (if any), Time, etc.\ntype LoopDeps struct {\n    // SpawnerFor maps agent name → Spawner. Returns nil for unknown agents.\n    // Production: passed in by the bridge file in cli package.\n    SpawnerFor func(agentName string) spawn.Spawner\n\n    // States persists/loads RunState. Caller passes a real StateStore in\n    // production; tests pass NewStateStoreWithDir(tempDir).\n    States *StateStore\n\n    // TranscriptDir is the directory where per-turn agent stdout logs are\n    // written. Format: <TranscriptDir>/<run-id>/turn-<N>-<agent>.log\n    TranscriptDir string\n\n    // VerboseOut, when non-nil, receives a tee of every per-turn agent\n    // stdout. nil disables the tee (logs still go to per-turn files).\n    VerboseOut io.Writer\n\n    // ProgressOut, when non-nil, receives \"Turn N · <agent>\" banners and\n    // \"Stance: <stance>\" trailers. nil suppresses progress output.\n    ProgressOut io.Writer\n\n    // Now returns the current time. Tests inject a fake clock.\n    // Defaults to time.Now if nil.\n    Now func() time.Time\n}\n\n// LoopInput carries everything runInvestigateLoop needs that isn't a hook.\ntype LoopInput struct {\n    RunID         string         // 12-hex\n    Topic         string\n    Agents        []string       // ordered, length >= 1\n    MaxTurns      int            // per-agent turn budget, default 3 if 0\n    Quorum        int            // approvals needed; 0 means len(Agents)\n    AlwaysPrompt  string\n    FindingsDoc   string         // absolute path\n    TimelineDoc   string         // absolute path\n    StartingSHA   string\n    PriorContext  string         // optional, e.g. ## Prior Entire Context\n    Resume        *RunState      // when non-nil, resume from this state\n}\n\n// LoopOutcome describes how the loop ended.\ntype LoopOutcome string\n\nconst (\n    OutcomeQuorum    LoopOutcome = \"quorum\"\n    OutcomeStalled   LoopOutcome = \"stalled\"\n    OutcomePaused    LoopOutcome = \"paused\"\n    OutcomeCancelled LoopOutcome = \"cancelled\"\n)\n\n// LoopResult is the loop's final report.\ntype LoopResult struct {\n    Outcome LoopOutcome\n    State   *RunState\n    Err     error // last per-turn spawn error, if any (informational; nil on clean Outcome)\n}\n\n// RunInvestigateLoop runs the round-robin investigation loop until it\n// reaches quorum, stalls, gets paused, or the context is cancelled.\nfunc RunInvestigateLoop(ctx context.Context, in LoopInput, deps LoopDeps) (LoopResult, error)\n```\n\n## Loop algorithm\n\n```\nstate := load-or-init RunState from in.Resume / in\ndefaults: if MaxTurns == 0, MaxTurns = 3; if Quorum == 0, Quorum = len(Agents)\nmaxOverallTurns := MaxTurns * len(Agents)\nconsecutiveFails := 0\nfor state.Turn < maxOverallTurns:\n    if ctx.Err() != nil: return Cancelled\n    agent := Agents[state.NextAgentIdx]\n    state.Turn++\n    if state.NextAgentIdx == 0: state.Round++ (round increments when we wrap to first agent — initial state.Round is 0, so first turn becomes round 1)\n\n    actually: simpler to compute Round = ((state.Turn - 1) / len(Agents)) + 1 — record this on the TurnStance\n\n    pre := hash findings + timeline\n    prompt := ComposeInvestigatePrompt(...)\n    env := AppendInvestigateEnv(os.Environ(), AppendOptions{\n        AgentName: agent, RunID: in.RunID, Round: round, Turn: state.Turn,\n        Topic: in.Topic, Prompt: prompt,\n        FindingsDoc: in.FindingsDoc, TimelineDoc: in.TimelineDoc,\n        StartingSHA: in.StartingSHA,\n    })\n    spawner := deps.SpawnerFor(agent); if nil → BLOCKED-style error: \"no spawner for agent %q\"\n    cmd := spawner.BuildCmd(ctx, env, prompt)\n    open per-turn log file: <TranscriptDir>/<RunID>/turn-<state.Turn>-<agent>.log\n    cmd.Stdout = MultiWriter(logFile, optional VerboseOut)\n    cmd.Stderr = same MultiWriter (per CLAUDE.md privacy: agents emit only their own output, no prompts/file bodies)\n    print progress banner \"Turn N · <agent>\"\n    err := cmd.Run()\n    close logFile\n    post := hash findings + timeline\n\n    stance, note := parseStanceFromTimeline(in.TimelineDoc, agent, state.Turn)\n    if err != nil:\n        consecutiveFails++\n        record TurnStance with stance=\"unknown\", note=\"spawn error: <err>\", append to state.Stances\n        save state\n        if consecutiveFails >= 2: return Paused\n        // advance idx, continue\n    else:\n        consecutiveFails = 0\n        record TurnStance{Round, Turn, Agent, Stance: stance, PlanChanged: pre.findings != post.findings, TimelineChanged: pre.timeline != post.timeline, Note: note}\n        save state\n        print progress trailer\n\n    state.NextAgentIdx = (state.NextAgentIdx + 1) % len(Agents)\n    save state\n\n    // Check quorum after wrapping to first agent (i.e., a complete round just ended)\n    if state.NextAgentIdx == 0:\n        if approveCountInLastRound(state) >= Quorum: return Quorum\n\nreturn Stalled\n```\n\nThe \"Round\" logic: marvin counts rounds as completed full passes through all agents. Match that. On the initial unrun state, `state.Round = 0`, `state.NextAgentIdx = 0`. After turn 1 by agents[0], `state.NextAgentIdx = 1`. After all agents have gone once, `state.NextAgentIdx wraps to 0` and we increment `state.Round` to 1, then check quorum.\n\nTo keep state recovery simple: persist `state.Round` as the **completed** round count. Set `state.Round = (state.Turn) / len(Agents)`. Always recompute on save.\n\n## Stance parsing\n\nThe agent edits the timeline file to add a block like:\n\n```\n## Turn 3 — claude-code\n\n**Stance:** approve\n\nI think this looks fine because ...\n```\n\nImplement `ParseStanceFromTimeline(timelinePath string, agent string, turn int) (stance string, note string, found bool)`:\n\n1. Read the file.\n2. Find a heading matching `## Turn <turn> — <agent>` (allow `—` em-dash, `--`, or `-` separators, allow extra whitespace).\n3. From that heading until the next `## ` heading or EOF, look for a line matching `**Stance:**\\s*(\\w[\\w-]*)` (case-insensitive `stance`).\n4. Stance is one of `approve`, `request-changes`, `abstain`. Anything else → `unknown`.\n5. If the heading is not found OR no Stance line is in the block → return `\"unknown\"` with note `\"timeline missing stance\"`.\n6. Returned `note` is empty string on success unless there's noteworthy info.\n\nMake this function exported and standalone-tested — no I/O dependencies beyond reading the file.\n\n## Hashing\n\nAdd a helper `hashDocs(findings, timeline string) docHashes` that returns a struct with two SHA-256 hex strings (or empty string when the file is missing or unreadable — log via slog Debug, never fail the loop).\n\n## Per-turn log file\n\nPath: `<TranscriptDir>/<RunID>/turn-<state.Turn>-<agent>.log`. `MkdirAll` the parent on first turn. Open with `os.O_CREATE | os.O_WRONLY | os.O_TRUNC` (each turn gets its own file, but tolerate re-runs by truncating). 0o640 file mode.\n\n## Tests in `loop_test.go`\n\nUse a fake spawner that mutates the timeline file and returns:\n\n```go\ntype fakeSpawner struct {\n    name string\n    onBuildCmd func(ctx context.Context, env []string, prompt string) *exec.Cmd\n}\nfunc (s *fakeSpawner) Name() string { return s.name }\nfunc (s *fakeSpawner) BuildCmd(ctx context.Context, env []string, prompt string) *exec.Cmd {\n    return s.onBuildCmd(ctx, env, prompt)\n}\n```\n\nFor each test, the fake's `onBuildCmd` returns a `*exec.Cmd` constructed with `exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"bash\", \"-c\", \"<script that appends a turn block to $ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_TIMELINE_DOC>\")`. The script can use `printf >> \"$timeline\"` to add the heading + Stance line.\n\nTests:\n1. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_QuorumReachedFirstRound`** — 3 agents, all approve in round 1; loop ends with `OutcomeQuorum`, state has 3 stances all `approve`.\n2. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_QuorumDefault`** — Quorum=0, 2 agents, both approve → quorum (default = len(Agents)).\n3. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_Stalled`** — 2 agents, MaxTurns=2, all return `request-changes`; after 4 turns, `OutcomeStalled`.\n4. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_PausedOnTwoFailures`** — fake spawner returns a script that exits 1 (using `exit 1`); after 2 consecutive failures, `OutcomePaused`.\n5. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_UnknownStanceWhenTimelineMissing`** — fake script doesn't touch the timeline; turn records stance `unknown`, loop continues.\n6. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_PersistsStateEachTurn`** — after each turn, a fresh StateStore.Load returns the latest TurnStance count.\n7. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_Resume`** — pre-seed RunState with NextAgentIdx=1 and 1 stance; resume; verify next agent in line is the second agent.\n8. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_PlanAndTimelineChangedFlags`** — fake script writes only the timeline (PlanChanged=false, TimelineChanged=true); verify recorded.\n9. **`TestRunInvestigateLoop_CancelledContext`** — ctx cancelled mid-turn; loop returns `OutcomeCancelled`.\n10. **`TestParseStanceFromTimeline`** — table test for: stance present (approve, request-changes, abstain), unknown stance keyword, missing heading, missing Stance line, em-dash vs `--` vs `-` separators, extra whitespace.\n\nFor tests on the bash one-liner approach: use `t.TempDir()` for findings/timeline/transcripts, `t.Skip` on Windows if necessary (`runtime.GOOS == \"windows\"` → skip; CI is Linux/macOS, this is fine).\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Read CLAUDE.md before starting.\n- DO NOT modify CLAUDE.md, commit, or touch files outside `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/`.\n- Tests must call `t.Parallel()` (the bash-spawn loop tests may need to be serial if file races appear; use unique TempDirs to keep them parallel).\n- Use `logging` package for diagnostics. Per CLAUDE.md privacy rules: never log prompts, file bodies, or commit messages — only operational metadata.\n- Don't import the review package or anything from cli package — investigate stays a leaf package.\n- Exec subprocesses must use `execx.NonInteractive` if available (look at `cmd/entire/cli/execx/`); if not relevant for plain bash spawns in tests, use `exec.CommandContext` directly. The production loop uses the Spawner abstraction; the test fake constructs its own Cmd via plain exec.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nmise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test -- ./cmd/entire/cli/investigate/...\n```\n\n## Reporting\n\nReport DONE / DONE_WITH_CONCERNS / BLOCKED / NEEDS_CONTEXT. Include files added, tests added, and verification output. List any concerns."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":225084,"output_tokens":16125,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":602},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":16125,"cache_read_input_tokens":225084,"cache_creation_input_tokens":602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":602,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Car5N6e6Aupvrn199rAQn","attributionSkill":"superpowers:subagent-driven-development","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"18422594-5e43-49d0-a8d2-8116178a8b3c","timestamp":"2026-05-09T00:50:57.356Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":