{"parentUuid":"18422594-5e43-49d0-a8d2-8116178a8b3c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019Jn4NC8RRmPmMnD4q2Gcgi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RDVV6GQA2PrrfVaUnMeKb3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement Task 6: fix + agentlaunch","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are implementing Task 6 of a larger plan: extract a shared `agentlaunch` package and create the `entire investigate fix` subcommand.\n\nWorking directory: /Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/entire-labs-investigate\n\n## Context\n\n`entire review --fix` resolves a saved review manifest, composes a prompt with the findings, and launches a normal coding agent session via `launchReviewFixAgent` (in `cmd/entire/cli/review/fix.go`). We need the equivalent for `entire investigate fix [<run-id>]`. Both should share the launch helper instead of duplicating it.\n\nThe launch helper currently:\n1. Resolves the agent via `agent.Get` and `agent.LauncherFor`.\n2. Calls `launcher.LaunchCmd(ctx, prompt)` to get an `*exec.Cmd`.\n3. Strips `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` from `cmd.Env` (or `os.Environ()` if cmd.Env is empty) using the local `withoutReviewEnv` helper.\n4. Runs the cmd, returning a friendly error on cancellation or non-zero exit.\n\nWe need to broaden the env-strip step to remove BOTH `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` AND `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` so a fix session never inherits provenance env from its parent.\n\nEarlier tasks already produced:\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/env.go` — `IsInvestigateEnvEntry` and `EnvSession`/etc constants.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/manifest.go` — `LocalManifest`, `LocalManifestStore` with `Write`, `List`, `FindByRunID`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/state.go` — `RunState`, `StateStore`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/issuelink.go` — irrelevant for this task.\n\n## What to do\n\n### 1. Create `cmd/entire/cli/agentlaunch/launch.go`\n\nMove the body of `launchReviewFixAgent` into this new package. Public API:\n\n```go\n// Package agentlaunch is the shared \"launch a normal coding agent session\n// with a composed prompt\" helper, used by `entire review --fix` and\n// `entire investigate fix`. Both commands feed accepted findings back into\n// a follow-up coding agent without spawning a review/investigate session\n// themselves.\npackage agentlaunch\n\nimport (\n    \"context\"\n)\n\n// LaunchFixAgent starts a normal coding agent session with the given\n// prompt. ENTIRE_REVIEW_* and ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_* env entries are stripped\n// from the child process so the fix session is not tagged as a review or\n// investigate.\n//\n// agentName must be a launchable agent registry name. Returns nil on clean\n// exit, or a wrapped error on cancellation / non-zero exit. Output / input\n// are connected to the calling process's stdio so the user can interact\n// with the fix session in their terminal.\nfunc LaunchFixAgent(ctx context.Context, agentName string, prompt string) error\n```\n\nThe implementation:\n1. `agent.Get(types.AgentName(agentName))` to resolve the agent.\n2. `agent.LauncherFor(ag.Name())` to get the interactive launcher (the one used today by `launchReviewFixAgent`).\n3. `launcher.LaunchCmd(ctx, prompt)` for the `*exec.Cmd`.\n4. Set `cmd.Stdin = os.Stdin`, `cmd.Stdout = os.Stdout`, `cmd.Stderr = os.Stderr` so the user sees the agent. Look at the current `launchReviewFixAgent` body to confirm this is what it does (it relies on `LaunchCmd` to set stdio, but verify).\n5. Strip env: `cmd.Env = withoutReviewOrInvestigateEnv(cmd.Env)` then if `cmd.Env` is empty, fall back to `withoutReviewOrInvestigateEnv(os.Environ())` (mirror the existing pattern).\n6. Run; wrap errors as today (`context.Canceled` → \"fix agent cancelled\", `*exec.ExitError` → \"fix agent exited with status %d\", else \"run fix agent: %w\").\n\nThe strip helper:\n```go\n// withoutReviewOrInvestigateEnv returns a copy of base with all\n// ENTIRE_REVIEW_* and ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_* entries rem