/entire/cli/investigate/cmd.go`\n\nThe cobra entry point. Mirror the structure of `review/cmd.go`:\n\n```go\n// Package investigate — see env.go for package-level rationale.\npackage investigate\n\n// Deps collects the runtime-injectable hooks NewCommand needs from the\n// parent cli package. Tests stub fields to drive branches that would\n// otherwise require a real TTY or enabled repo.\ntype Deps struct {\n    GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled func(ctx context.Context) []types.AgentName\n    NewSilentError              func(err error) error\n\n    // SpawnerFor maps an agent name → Spawner (claude-code, codex, gemini-cli).\n    // Returns nil for non-launchable agents. Wired by investigate_bridge.go in\n    // a later task.\n    SpawnerFor func(agentName string) spawn.Spawner\n\n    // LaunchFix delegates to agentlaunch.LaunchFixAgent in production. Tests\n    // inject a stub.\n    LaunchFix func(ctx context.Context, agentName string, prompt string) error\n\n    // PriorEntireContextFn returns the \"## Prior Entire Context\" body for\n    // the seed-doc scaffold. Production may run `entire search` or read\n    // checkpoints; tests pass nil to skip the block.\n    PriorEntireContextFn func(ctx context.Context, topic string) string\n\n    // AttachCmd is the optional `entire investigate attach <session-id>`\n    // subcommand. Wired in a later task.\n    AttachCmd *cobra.Command\n}\n\n// NewCommand returns the `entire investigate` cobra command.\nfunc NewCommand(deps Deps) *cobra.Command\n```\n\n### Flag set\n\nPer the plan §1, the command surface is:\n\n```\nentire investigate                        # Run with config (or first-run picker)\nentire investigate [seed-doc]             # Use seed file as starting findings\nentire investigate --topic \"<question>\"\nentire investigate --issue-link <url>\nentire investigate --agents <csv>         # Override configured agents\nentire investigate --max-turns N          # Default 3\nentire investigate --quorum N             # Default 0 = all agents\nentire investigate --output <path>        # Override findings doc location\nentire investigate --continue <run-id>    # Resume\nentire investigate --edit                 # Re-open the config picker\nentire investigate --findings             # Browse local manifests\nentire investigate --verbose              # Tee per-turn stdout to terminal\n```\n\nPlus the `fix` subcommand: `entire investigate fix [<run-id>]`.\n\n### Validation rules\n\n- At most one of `[seed-doc]`, `--topic`, `--issue-link` per run.\n- `--continue` mutually exclusive with seed/topic/issue inputs.\n- `--edit` and `--findings` mutually exclusive with each other and with the run path.\n- Every agent in the resolved list must have a non-nil `SpawnerFor` AND be in `GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled`.\n\n### Run flow\n\n`runInvestigate(ctx, cmd, args, flags, deps)`:\n\n1. Pre-flight: must be in a git repo (`paths.WorktreeRoot`).\n2. If `--edit`: call `RunInvestigateConfigPicker`, save settings, return.\n3. If `--findings`: call `runInvestigateFindings` (see below), return.\n4. If `--continue <run-id>`: load existing RunState from `StateStore.Load`. If not found, error. Otherwise, recover topic/agents/max-turns/quorum from RunState, skip seed doc bootstrap, jump to loop.\n5. Otherwise (fresh run):\n   a. Load settings (`settings.Load`). If `Investigate` is unset, prompt first-run setup, run picker, save.\n   b. Resolve agents: `--agents` override > settings.Investigate.Agents.\n   c. Resolve max-turns/quorum: flags > settings.Investigate.\n   d. Verify each resolved agent has a Spawner AND hooks installed. If not, error: \"agent %q is not launchable (run `entire configure --agent %s` first)\" or \"spawner missing for %q\".\n   e. Resolve HEAD SHA: `git rev-parse HEAD` (use `runGit` style helper or shell to git via `exec.CommandContext` — check `cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go` for `currentHeadSHA` and copy the pattern; if accessible, import it… actually `currentHeadSHA` is unexported in review. Replicate it locally in investigate as a tiny helper `currentHeadSHA(ctx, repoRoot)`.).\n   f. Generate `runID` (12 hex chars, `crypto/rand` + `hex.EncodeToString`).\n   g. Resolve topic + seed:\n      - Positional `[seed-doc]`: read file. Topic = `DeriveTopicFromSeed(body, filename)`.\n      - `--topic`: topic = flag value. Seed = nil.\n      - `--issue-link`: `ResolveIssueLink(ctx, url)`. Topic = result.Topic. Seed = result.SeedDoc bytes.\n   h. Compute slug = `SlugifyTopic(topic)`.\n   i. Decide findings doc location: `--output` > `.entire/investigations/<slug>.md` (within the worktree). Timeline = `<findings>-timeline.md`.\n   j. Call `Bootstrap(ctx, BootstrapInput{...})` to write the docs (with `PriorEntireContext = deps.PriorEntireContextFn(ctx, topic)` if non-nil, else \"\").\n   k. Initialize RunState; persist via StateStore.Save.\n   l. Print a banner: \"Investigating: <topic> (run <runID>)\".\n6. Build LoopDeps, then call `RunInvestigateLoop(ctx, LoopInput{...}, LoopDeps{...})`.\n7. After loop returns:\n   - Build a LocalManifest with run-id, topic, slug, agents, outcome, last stance per agent (from `result.State.Stances`), starting-sha, worktree-path, findings/timeline doc paths, started/ended.\n   - `LocalManifestStore.Write(ctx, manifest)`. Log on failure but don't error — the docs themselves are the deliverable.\n   - Print a footer: outcome line + how to run `entire investigate fix <run-id>`.\n8. Return nil on success or a wrapped error.\n\n### Sub-commands wired\n\n- `fix`: a subcommand `entire investigate fix [<run-id>]` that calls `RunFix(ctx, FixInput, FixDeps)` from `fix.go`. Build `FixDeps` from `deps`. Add this subcommand on `NewCommand`.\n- `attach`: passed in via `deps.AttachCmd` (Task 9 will wire it). If non-nil, `cmd.AddCommand(deps.AttachCmd)`.\n\n### 2. `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/picker.go`\n\nFirst-run config picker.\n\n```go\n// RunInvestigateConfigPicker shows a multi-select of eligible agents and\n// prompts for max-turns / quorum. Saves the resulting InvestigateConfig\n// into settings.\n//\n// Eligibility: agent has a Spawner AND has hooks installed. Non-spawnable\n// agents (cursor, opencode, factoryai-droid, copilot-cli) are filtered out\n// at the Spawner check.\nfunc RunInvestigateConfigPicker(\n    ctx context.Context,\n    out io.Writer,\n    spawnerFor func(agentName string) spawn.Spawner,\n    getAgentsWithHooksInstalled func(ctx context.Context) []types.AgentName,\n) (*settings.InvestigateConfig, error)\n\n// ConfirmFirstRunSetup prints a banner explaining we're configuring before\n// running, gets y/N, returns true on yes. Mirrors review's ConfirmFirstRunSetup.\nfunc ConfirmFirstRunSetup(ctx context.Context, out io.Writer) bool\n\n// Helper that filters and sorts the eligible-agent list for picker display.\ntype agentChoice struct {\n    Name  string\n    Label string\n}\n\nfunc eligibleAgentsForInvestigate(ctx context.Context, spawnerFor func(string) spawn.Spawner, hookInstalled []types.AgentName) []agentChoice\n```\n\nUse `huh` (charm.land/huh/v2) for the picker, mirroring how `review/picker.go` does it. Wrap forms in `WithAccessible(true)` if `ACCESSIBLE` env is set (search the existing picker for the pattern; usually a small `isAccessibleMode()` helper or `NewAccessibleForm`).\n\n### 3. `cmd/entire/cli/investigate/findings.go`\n\nThe `--findings` browser.\n\n```go\n// runInvestigateFindings handles `entire investigate --findings`: lists\n// LocalManifests for browsing. In a TTY, shows a huh selector and prints\n// the chosen manifest's details. In non-TTY mode, prints a plain list with\n// \"fix\" command hints.\nfunc runInvestigateFindings(ctx context.Context, cmd *cobra.Command, silentErr func(error) error) error\n```\n\nMirror `review/fix.go`'s `runReviewFindings` for shape.\n\n### 4. Tests\n\nCobra command tests are notoriously tricky. Use the same approach `review/cmd_test.go` uses:\n- Build a `Deps` with stub fields.\n- Call `cmd.SetArgs([]string{...})` and `cmd.Execute()`.\n- Assert error / output / side effects.\n\nTests to add in `cmd_test.go`:\n\n- `TestNewCommand_RejectsConflictingInputs` — args `[\"foo.md\", \"--topic=bar\"]` returns error.\n- `TestNewCommand_RejectsContinueWithSeed` — `--continue=abc --topic=bar` returns error.\n- `TestNewCommand_FixSubcommand` — `entire investigate fix --help` is rendered.\n- `TestNewCommand_AttachSubcommand` — when `Deps.AttachCmd` is set, `--help` lists it.\n- `TestNewCommand_EditCallsPicker` — pass a stub picker via Deps; `--edit` triggers it.\n- `TestNewCommand_FindingsCallsBrowser` — pass a stub manifest store; `--findings` lists.\n- `TestNewCommand_NotInGitRepoReturnsError` — chdir to a non-repo dir and run; expect actionable error.\n- `TestNewCommand_AgentsFlagOverrideUsed` — when `--agents` is set, it overrides settings (verify by inspecting state of LoopInput passed to a stub LoopRun — see below).\n\nFor the loop dispatch you'll want to inject the loop runner (the function that runs the loop) via Deps so tests don't need real spawners. Add to `Deps`:\n\n```go\n// LoopRun, when non-nil, replaces RunInvestigateLoop. Tests inject a stub\n// to capture LoopInput and return a canned LoopResult.\nLoopRun func(ctx context.Context, in LoopInput, ldeps LoopDeps) (LoopResult, error)\n```\n\nDefault to `RunInvestigateLoop` when nil.\n\nTests for picker/findings:\n\n- `TestRunInvestigateConfigPicker_NoEligibleAgents` — spawnerFor returns nil for all; expect actionable error.\n- `TestRunInvestigateConfigPicker_FiltersNonInstalled` — only one of two has hooks; selector lists only one.\n  (Use a stub for the huh form via `WithProgramOptions(tea.WithInput(...), tea.WithOutput(...))` if needed; or inject a `pickerFormFn` into the picker so tests can swap the form. Mirror the testing pattern in `review/picker_test.go` and `review/multipicker_test.go`.)\n- `TestRunInvestigateFindings_PrintsListNonTTY` — write 2 manifests to a temp store, call the function, check stdout has both run-ids.\n- `TestR